	string asis;------------------------------------------;; Equates from procedure ;;------------------------------------------CheckMach	equ $fe1f	;Monitor Routine to	check machine typep16flag	equ $E100BDLastDev	equ $bf30ZP	equ $1000	; where ProDOS 8 "loader" goes.;-----------------------------------------------;;   Imported addresses;;-----------------------------------------------	IMPORT DES;-----------------------------------------------;;   Forward addresses and entries;;-----------------------------------------------**************************************************************************  Logon.asm**  Copyright Apple Computer Inc., 1987*  All rights reserved**  Written by	Richard B. Hoiberg*  Created: 11-Oct-86**  Modification history:**  14-Jul-87	Fixed stack bug in error handling -	RGKKSA003 (rbh)*  15-Jul-87	Fixed bug in chooser server with backward beq longer than*	127.  (rbh)*  29-Jul-87	Added changes for the new Message routines in the console*	driver (rbh)*  30-Jul-87	Escaping from the volume list now exits the program without*	mounting selected volumes. (rbh)*  2-Aug-87	Fixed bug in Error loop, where GetServerParms got called*	unintentionally. (rbh)*  2-Aug-87	Changes made so that one volume could be mounted correctly. (rbh)*  6-Aug-87	Changed the input routine so that return in the name field acts the*	same as a Tab.*  6-Aug-87	Added current zone to select zone list.*  20-Aug-87	Fixed stack for continous Rebooting over the network**  28-Sept-87	Move the FINaming call to ByeBye so that the Naming*	convention would always be set to ProDOS Naming.*  28-Sept-87	Set the name of a guest to <Any User> using the FIName*	call.*  11-Oct-87	Modified to allow execution in any bank with 65816.*	Should be called in 8-bit native mode.  (Mark Day)*  15-Apr-88	Converted to MAX source (msd)*  18-Apr-88	Modified ProDOS 8 "launch" routine to run at $1000 (msd)*  29-Apr-88	Verifies volume name during update name (msd)*	Version number changed to 1.1d2*  25-May-88	Two-byte decrements were decrementing the high byte*	when low byte turned to 0 (instead of $FF).  Located*	in LaunchAppl at LA3 and in ItemSel at NS1.  If an invalid*	session number error is returned in MountVol, the "Server*	not responding" message is displayed instead of "This*	volume does not have a proper ProDOS pathname".  (msd)*  27-May-88	Trying to work-around a bug that causes partial pathnames*	not to work after quitting logon.  Do GetPrefix then*	SetPrefix after setting short naming mode.*  2-Jun-88	From "Select a file server" menu, when you got a*	"Server not responding" message, it would look for*	servers again and let you select one.  When you*	selected Registered User or Guest, it would go back*	to looking for servers.  This has been fixed (MSD).*	Version is now 1.1d5.*  20-Oct-88	Restructred for conditional assemblies (RBH)*  25-Jan-89	Trying to make sure page-wrap problems don't happen.*	Code is typically of the form:*	  lda #<address+n*	  sta ...*	  lda #>address*	  sta ...*	You usually want #>address+n.  This will cause*	problems when address and address+n are in*	different pages.  (MSD)*  7-Feb-89	The code to check for a volume password was using*	(StgPtr2),y without setting Y.  Changed to (StgPtr2)*	since StgPtr2 points to the password flag at that time.*  19-Nov-90	Fixed some problem with >128 zone names where the index*	into the string pointer array is only one byte (so an*	ASL to convert it into a word pointer loses the upper*	bit).  (MSD)*  13-Dec-90	Fixed LaunchAppl to check the file type of the file it is*	about to launch.  It must be type $FF (ProDOS SYS file).*	Version is 1.3d2.  (MSD)*  04-Jun-91	Starting to make changes to allow you to mount volumes*	without having to mount a user volume.  This makes us*	work better with File Sharing.  Version is 1.3d3.*  12-Jun-91	Version 1.3d4.  The server and volume lists are now sorted.*	All lists now uses keyboard navigation.*  13-Jun-91	Version 1.3d5.  ProDOS 16 booting now includes both the*	GS/OS and ProDOS 8 code.  A new flag, BootOS, is used to*	decide at run-time (as opposed to compile time) which*	code path to take.  BootOS is 1 for GS/OS, 2 for ProDOS 8.*  18-Jun-91 MSD	Version 1.4d6.  ProDOS 16 application (and CDA) version*	now allows no user volume to be mounted.  Remove sorting*	of volume list since it doesn't sort the array of selection*	flags (telling which is a user volume, for example).*	The version is now 1.4xx to avoid confusion with the*	separately maintained version 1.3 for Double Exposure.*	Retry for lookup of servers changed to 16 times, every second.*  25-Jun-91	Don't check for the router's node number being non-zero before*	trying a GetMyZone or GetZoneList.  On 976, you can have zones*	even though you don't have a router on your local network.*	Version changed to 1.4d7.*  09-Jul-91 MSD	Changing the retry interval and count for the GetMyZone call to*	better handle the case where there are zones.  Version changed to*	1.4d8.*  11-Jul-91 MSD	Conditionally assembled out registering of a user name from the*	GS boot blocks (since the GS uses the actual name structure, not*	a copy like the Bullwinkle card does).*  06-Aug-91 MSD	FindCard fixed to bypass the GS's built-in LocalTalk firmware and*	continue looking for a real card.**  27-Aug-91 MSD	The ByeBye routine for P16 boot blocks branches back to Logon which*	destroys the BootOS flag.  Added new label "LogRestart16" to branch*	back to.  Version changed to 1.4d9.*   7-Feb-92 MSD	Changed copyright dates to include 1992.  Changed version to 1.4 final.*  31-Aug-92 MSD	Changed version to 1.5d1.  It now checks the error from the GetInfo call*	that is made when the program first runs.  If there was an error, then*	an alert is displayed and the program quits.  Fixes bug #1035511.*  25-Nov-92 DAL	Added a "Looking for AppleTalk zones" message while looking for zones.*	Added a store of $AA to location $00 on getting a generic error.*   2-Apr-93 DAL	Changed version to 1.5 final.**************************************************************************Home	equ $FC58CrHB	equ $8dTabHB	equ $89mli	equ $BF00StgPtr	equ $83StgPtr2	equ $85BasStart	equ $2000IOBuff	equ $bb00OurPath	equ $280RomIn	equ $c082SetVid	equ $fe93SetKbd	equ $fe89RomID	equ $fbc0Cout	equ $fdedch	equ $24Speaker	equ $c030Clr80Vid	equ $c00cSetAltChar	equ $c00fClr80Col	equ $c000SelPtr	equ $feNull	equ 0MachId	equ $bf98Open	equ $c8Write	equ $cbSetMark	equ $ceClose	equ $ccGetEof	equ $d1Set_Prefix	equ $c6GetPrefix	equ $c7Quit	equ $65ReadBlock	equ $80Flush	equ $cdGetFInfo	equ $c4Online	equ $c5Read	equ $caMailFlagOffset	equ 276PathOffset	equ 269PfxOffset	equ 198PrOffset	equ 99NameOffset	equ 133NameLen	equ 31Logon	IF OSFlag = 192 THEN	sta BootOS	; remember which OS we're booting into		; it will be positive for GS/OS	clc	xce	; force native mode!	rep #$30	; long mode so we can save S	longa on	longi on	tsc	; stack in A (C)	sta Stack16	; save off stack at entry	sep #$30	; back to 8-bit mode	longa off	longi off	ENDIFLogRestart16	stz ZoneFlag	stz SkipFlag	ATCall GetInfo	bcc @installed	; no error, AppleTalk is installed	ldx #16	; "AppleTalk must be installed"	ldy #$80	; OK button only (no Cancel)	jsr ErrorHandler	jmp ByeBye	; Log out and exit@installed	lda ABridge		; 25-Jun-91 MSD		; Don't check the router node.  Try		; the GetMyZone and handle the error		; if we get one (might work with 976).	sta BridgeNode	ATCall GetMyZone	bcs @LI2	;oops! the GetMyZone call failed, time to punt	lda #$80	sta ZoneFlag	;there are zones	lda #0	;push the offset	pha	;	PushWord #ZoneName	;push the destination	PushWord #ReplyBuff	;push the source	_MoveStr@LI2	WriteChar RstWind	;restore the window	WriteChar ClrWind	FrameRect FrameParms1	SViewPort MainWindow	WriteCStr Title	ReptChar TitLineMain	stz OtherSrvrFlg	; MSD: don't need to get another server anymore	jsr FindServers	cmp #Return	beq @SaveNode	bit ZoneFlag	bmi @NewZone	jmp ByeBye@SaveNode	jsr SaveNode	;get the entity address, and check version and UAM	beq @Login	;no error, so Logon	to the file Server.	bra Main	;select another server@NewZone	jsr ChangeZone	;get another zone	cmp #Return	beq @NZ1	jmp ByeBye	;get a list of Servers from the new zone@NZ1	bit ZoneFlag	bpl Main	jsr TheNewZone	bra Main@Login		;	IF OSFlag = 0 then	jsr GetUserName	;get the user name here from the ATINIT	file	Else	stz NameBuffer	EndIF	lda #0	;zero length AFP Login packets are not sent	jsr CheckLogin	;across network, just checking for existing session	beq @Main3	;no error means we have not logged on to this server		;we have already logged on to this server		;to fix an non updated Toucan disk	cmp #Return	beq @Main2	;if it was a return, give him a volume list		;not return so an Escape was pressed	ldx MatchNum	;check to see if there is only one server	cpx #1	;if there is only one server and Escape	bne @Main1	;was pressed, then there are more zones	bra @NewZone	;get this boy a new	zone@Main1	bra Main	;get this dude a new server in this zone!@Main2	jsr SaveSess	;return was pressed, let him mount/unmount volumes	bra ByeBye	;all done@Main3	jsr GetSelection	;see how the user wants to logon	cmp #Return	beq @Main5	bit SkipFlag	bpl @Main4	jmp ByeBye@Main4		; 	stz OtherSrvrFlg	;clear another server flag	jmp Main@Main5	lda SelIndex	sta MySel@Main6		; 	bit OtherSrvrFlg	bmi @Main4	bit AuthFlag	;test authflag	bmi @Main3	lda MySel	cmp #1	beq @Main7	cmp #2	beq @Main8@Main7		; 	stz AuthFlag	jsr DoGetInput	bcc @LogAgain	jmp @Main3@Main8		; 	lda #$80	sta AuthFlag@LogAgain		; 	jsr DoLogon	bne @Main6	IF OSFLAG = 0 then 	lda MySel	cmp #3	bne @Main9	jsr ChangePass	;Change the password	jmp @Main3	EndIF@Main9	jsr SaveSess	beq @Main10	;if zero, all went well	cmp #$80	;check for a returned value of $80	beq @Main4	;if it is, then get	new server	jsr LogMeOut	;returned value was	$c0, escape was pressed	bra ByeBye@Main10	;	IF (OSFlag = 128) then	jmp LaunchAppl	;Prodos8 System application to ProDOS quit	EndIF	IF (OSFlag = 192) then	lda BootOS	dea	; was it 1 (GS/OS)?	beq @rts	; yes, so just return to Fizzy	jmp LaunchAppl	; do this if we're booting P8@rts	rts	; return to GS/OS boot logon	EndIF*ByeBye		; 	IF OSFlag = 128 then	jsr LogMeOut	jmp LogRestart	; else do ProDOS 8 restart	EndIF		IF OSFLag = 192 then	jsr LogMeOut	; make sure I'm logged out	clc	xce	; force native mode!	rep #$30	; long mode to restore S	longa on	longi on	lda Stack16	; get stack at entry	tcs	; and restore it	sep #$30	; back to 8-bit mode	longa off	longi off	brl LogRestart16	; go back and log on againStack16	dc.w 0	; save area for stack pointer on entryBootOS	dc.b 0	; tells us which OS we're booting into		; 1 = GS/OS, 2 = ProDOS 8	EndIF	IF OSFlag = 0 Then		; 	stz AuthFlag	;clear the Authorization flag, not a guest	jsr CheckMail	;check for mail	stz QuitParm+1	;clear the ProDOS 8	enhanced quit call	cld	;msd: clean up screen when launched	lda RomIn	;msd: as a ProDOS 8	application	jsr SetVid	jsr SetKbd	jsr Home	sta Clr80Vid	sta SetAltChar	sta Clr80Col	lda #<Prefix	;MSD: Workaround for bug where	sta SetPrefix+1	; ProDOS 8 doesn't understand the	lda #>Prefix	; prefix set during	long naming mode.	sta SetPrefix+2	; (start by pointing to buffer for	jsr mli	;  the prefix to be	returned).	dc.b $C7	dc.w SetPrefix	; Do GetPrefix and SetPrefix	bcs @PQ1	; to force ProDOS 8	to understand	jsr mli	; the prefix.  But don't do a	dc.b $C6	; SetPrefix if the GetPrefix failed.	dc.w SetPrefix@PQ1	jsr mli	;do the ProDOS quit	DC.B Quit	DC.W QuitParm	ENDIF		IF OSFlag = 64 Then		;	rts	EndIF*GetSelection		jsr ClearWindow	bit SkipFlag	bpl @GS1	WriteCStr Prompt9	bra @GS2@GS1		; 	WriteCStr Prompt1@GS2	stz AuthFlag	;clear the Authorization flag	ldx #5	stx SelXPos	;set the current x select position	ldx #3	stx SelYPos	ldx #1	stx Increment	stx SelIndex	lda #StrArray	sta StgArrayPtr	lda #>StrArray	sta StgArrayPtr+1	lda #2	;set this to 3 for change password option	sta ArrayCnt	sta ListOptByte	ListHandler ListParms	rtsLaunchAppl		;	IF (OSFlag = 128) or (OSFlag = 192) then	jsr CheckMail	;check for mail and	load ATINIT	sec	;calculate position	in the file	lda EOFPntr	;where the printer tuple is	sbc #PrOffset	;	sta PrName	;store in the PMSetPrinter parm list	sta StgPtr	lda EOFPntr+1	;do the high byte	sbc #>PrOffset	;	sta PrName+1	;	sta StgPtr+1	;need to use zero page to move the	lda StgPtr	;Printer Flag Byte	bne LA3	;decrement string pointer by one	dec StgPtr+1	;both the high and low bytesLA3	dec StgPtr	;msd: decrement fixed	ldy #0	;get the printer flag byte	lda (StgPtr),y	;	sta theflag	;and store in in the PMSetPrinter parm list	ATCall setprint	;set the printer name	sec	lda EOFPntr	sbc #PfxOffset	sta SetPrefix+1	lda EOFPntr+1	sbc #>PfxOffset	sta SetPrefix+2	sec	lda EOFPntr	sbc #<PathOffset	sta StgPtr	sta GetFInfoParm+1	sta QuitParm+2	lda EOFPntr+1	sbc #>PathOffset	sta StgPtr+1	sta GetFInfoParm+2	sta QuitParm+3* SET UP THE PATH TO FIND THE REST OF THE FILES	ldy #0	lda (StgPtr),y	tax	bne PathMuv	jmp ATOpenErrPathMuv	sta OurPath,yMuvLup	iny	lda (StgPtr),y	sta OurPath,y	dex	bne MuvLup	jsr mli	DC.B GetFInfo	DC.W GetFInfoParm	bcc LA2	jmp FileOpenErrLA2;; MSD 13-Dec-90: If the filetype is not SYS, put up a message and stop.; --->;	lda GetFInfoParm+4	; filetype	cmp #$FF	; SYS?	beq @isSYS	; yes, continue launch	ldx #24	; "not a ProDOS 8 app"	ldy #$80	; OK button only (no Cancel)	jsr ErrorHandler	jmp ByeBye	; Log out and try again@isSYS; <---; End of MSD 13-Dec-90 change.;	jsr DrawBox	;	WriteChar Return	;	WriteCStr LaunchStart ;Put up our prompt	WriteChar Return	;One line	WriteChar Return	;two lines	jsr PathProc	;and the path that we are launching	jsr mli	DC.B $c6	DC.W SetPrefix	bcc LA1	jsr PathOpenErr	bra LA2LA1	IF OSFlag=128 THEN	jsr RegisterName	ENDIFDoIt	ldx #00	;ELSE NEW INDEX TO 0MovLP	lda ZPLabel,X	;MOVING LOADER CODE	TO PAGE ZERO	sta zp,X	;ONE AT A TIME	inx	;NEXT ONE	cpx #LoaderLen	;WAS THAT THE LAST ONE	bne MovLP	;TAKEN IF NOT	jmp zp	;GIVE THE SHOW TO LOADERFileOpenErr		; 	cmp #$4e	bne FOE1	ldx #23	;do message number 23 - access error	bra FOE3FOE1	cmp #$46	beq FOE4	cmp #$44	bne FOE2FOE4	ldx #5	;do message number 5 - file not found	bra FOE3FOE2		; 	cmp #$45	;was the error volume not found?	bne FOE9	ldy #2FOE8	lda OurPath,y	cmp #'/'	beq FOE7	iny	bra FOE8FOE7		; 	sty OurPath	ldx #26	ldy #0	;if the file is not	found, maybe the wrong	bra FOE5	;volumes were mounted.FOE9	ldx #6	;unknown file open err - genericFOE3	ldy #$80FOE5	jsr ErrorHandler	cmp #Escape	;if escape was pressed, mount a differnt volume	bne FOE6	;if return, exit the program	jsr SaveSess	;	cmp #$c0	beq FOE6	jmp LaunchAppl	;try a new launchFOE6		; 	jmp ByeByePathOpenErr	ldx #11	ldy #$80	jsr ErrorHandler		;default prefix = path minus application nameDefPrefix		; 	ldy #0	;back up from the end of the string	lda (StgPtr),y	;until we reach a backslash	tax	;	tay	;PrefixLup	lda (StgPtr),y	cmp #'/'	;is it a backslash	beq NewPrefix	;this is our new prefix length	dey	dex	bne PrefixLupNewPrefix		; ;length of the default prefix is in x	register	ldy #0	;zero y register for indexing	txa	;store the length of the new prefix	sta Prefix,yMuvPfx	iny	lda (StgPtr),y	sta Prefix,y	dex	bne MuvPfx	lda #<Prefix	sta SetPrefix+1	lda #>Prefix	sta SetPrefix+2	rts		IF OSFlag=128 THENRegisterName		; 	lda #9	pha	;offset by 9	sta MovOffset	PushWord #ArrayBuff	;set up the zero page pointers for Register Name	PushWord #NameBuffer	;	_MoveStr	;move the string	lda NameBuffer	clc	;calculate the next offset	adc MovOffset	;	inc a	;take into account for the string length	sta MovOffset	;this is the next offsetDoType	sec	;check to see the Machine type	jsr CheckMach	;this monitor routine has a special purpose	bcs TwoE	;if the carry is set, it is a //e	lda MovOffset	pha	PushWord #ArrayBuff	;set up the zero page pointers for Register Name	PushWord #GSType	;	_MoveStr	;to make the name tuple	lda GSType	bra DoRegName	;TwoE		; 	lda MovOffset	pha	PushWord #ArrayBuff	;set up the zero page pointers for Register Name	PushWord #TwoEType	;	_MoveStr	;to make the name tuple	lda TwoETypeDoRegName		; 	clc	;calculate the next offset	adc MovOffset	inc a	;take into account for the string length	pha	;this is the next offset	PushWord #ArrayBuff	;set up the zero page pointers for Register Name	PushWord #MyZone	;	_MoveStr	;to make the name tuple	ATCall RegstrName	;	bcc alldone	;if the carry is clear, it was successful	jsr DeriveName	;derive a new name	bcs alldone	;if carry is set we	have already tried 99 times	jmp RegisterName	;do it againalldone	rts	;finally doneDeriveName		; 	stz NoNameFlag	;clear the NoName Flag	ldx NameBuffer	;get the last byte in the name buffer	lda NameBuffer,x	;	cmp #'>'	;see if the last character is a ">"	bne DN1	;if not, dont set NoNameFlag	lda #$80	;here we set the high bit 	sta NoNameFlag	;to indicate No Name or Any UserDN1		; ;	lda DeriveCnt	;get the Count	bne DN2	;if not zero, we dont need to add one to 	jsr AddOne	;this string	bra DN3	;this is the first pass at derivationDN2	cmp #9	;is the count 9?	bne DN3	;no, so check for 99	jsr AddOne	;it was 9, so add a	character for "10"DN3		; ;	cmp #99	;is the count 99?	bne DN4	;it wasnt so update	the string	sec	;99 times, give it up!	rtsDN4		; 	ldx NameBuffer	;get the Length of the string	bit NoNameFlag	;check for No Name	bpl DN5	;if not X is not decremented	dex	;DN5	inc NameBuffer,x	;add one to the ascii character in string	lda NameBuffer,x	;get the character	cmp #$3A	;is it an Ascii ':'?	bne DNDun	;if not, we are done	lda #$30	;it was, so we had wrap around	sta NameBuffer,x	;update for the right ascii character	dex	;	inc NameBuffer,x	;and increment the ten position character DNDun	inc DeriveCnt	;update the DeriveCnt	clc	rtsAddOne		; ;add the "0" character to the string	pha	;the Derivation count is in the accumulator	cmp #9	;is the count 9?	bne AO2	;if not, branch here without changes    	lda NameBuffer	;it is so add another character to the string	cmp #NameLen	;is the length 31?	beq AO1	;if it is, we will need to truncate	inc a	;add one to the accumulator	inc NameBuffer	;add one to the string lengthAO1	tax	;to the X regsiter	bit NoNameFlag	;check the NoNameFlag	bpl AO4	;if it is plus, then there is not the ">" at the end	dex	;back up one character for No Name - ">"AO4	lda #$2f	;init the count for	two bytes	sta NameBuffer,x	;store $2f here	dex	;	lda #$31	;	sta NameBuffer,x	;and $31 here	bra AODun	;to the bottom of the loopAO2		; 	lda NameBuffer	;get the length of the string in NameBuffer	cmp #NameLen	;is it 31?	beq AO3	;if so, the string does not need to be incremented	inc a	;increment a	inc NameBuffer	;and the stringAO3		; 	tax	;into the x register	bit NoNameFlag	;check for NoName -	">"	bpl AO6	;if not, store at current x postion 	dex	;it is No Name so, decrement by oneAO6	lda #$30	;store $30 at the postion pointed to by	X	sta NameBuffer,x	;AODun		; ;	bit NoNameFlag	;is this still No Name?	bpl AO5	;if not, were done!	lda #'>'	;the last character	is the - ">"	ldx NameBuffer	;	sta NameBuffer,x	;update the last character in the stringAO5	pla	;and restore the accumulator	rts	;bye, byeFindCard		; 	jsr Check2e	;check to see if the //e is properly configured	lda #$f9	;it came back so we	are ok	sta cardptr	lda #$c7	sta cardptr+1NxtSlot	ldy #3ckloop	lda (cardptr),y	cmp idtbl,y	bne NoMatch	dey	bpl ckloop	ldy #4	lda (cardptr),y	beq NoMatch	; 6-Aug-91 MSD: bypass GS's built-in LocalTalk	cmp #1	bne NoGo	clc	rtsNoMatch		; 	dec cardptr+1	lda cardptr+1	cmp #$c0	;are we finished scanning the slots?	bne NxtSlotNoGo	sec	rtsCheck2e		; 	sec	;check to see if the machine is a //gs	jsr CheckMach	;	bcc IIeGood	;if so, we are done	lda #0	;load the accumulator	inc a	;this is a 65C02 instruction	beq NoGood2e	;if zero, this is a	6502	lda MachID	;get the ProDOS MachID	and #$F2	;clear the unwanted	bits	cmp #%10110010	;this should be the	result 128K, 80 Col	bne NoGood2e	lda RomID	;check for enhanced	roms	cmp #$e1	;debugger roms	beq IIeGood	cmp #$E0	;is the byte E0?	bne NoGood2e	;Off we go to display the messageIIeGood	clc	;clear the carry flag	rts	;we have passed the	testNoGood2e		; 	jsr Home	;clear the screen	jsr DrawInvBox	;draw a box for display	ldy #7	ldx #5	jsr gopos	;set the cursor position	lda #<qmsg1	ldx #>qmsg1	ldy qmsg1len	jsr printblk	;print the message	ldy #9	ldx #5	jsr GoPos	lda #<qmsg2	ldx #>qmsg2ge1		; 	ldy qmsg2len	jsr printblk	;print the messagenopass		; 	jsr DobellNoGo2	jmp NoGo2PrintBlk		; 	sta stgptr	;SET UP ZERO PAGE	STX StgPtr+1	;	sty BlockLen	;SAVE THE NUMBER OF	CHARACTERS TO PRINT	ldy #0	;START WITH CHARACTER #1PLOOP	lda (StgPtr),Y	;GET THE CHARACTER	ORA #$80	;SET THE HIGH BIT 	jsr cout	;OUTPUT TO SCREEN	iny	;INCREMENT Y REGISTER	cpy BlockLen	;CHECK TO SEE IF WERE AT THE END OF BLK	bne PLoop	;IF NOT CONTINUE	inc ch	;add one to ch, not	sure why??	rts	;IF SO, WE ARE DONEgopos		; 	dey	;Setup the Y screen	coordinates from 1-24, not the	tya	;monitior 0-23.	jsr vtab	;set the vertical position	dex	;Setup the X screen	coordinates from 1-80, not the	stx ch	;set the horizontal	position.	rts	;and returnDobell		; 	LDA #$40	;DURATION	STA B_LNGTHBELL_1	LDA #$02	;SHORT DELAY	JSR B_WAIT	STA Speaker	LDA #$24	;LONG DELAY	JSR B_WAIT	STA Speaker	DEC B_LNGTH	BNE BELL_1	RTSDrawInvBox		; 	lda #10	sta DrawCnt	ldy #5	sty Ypos	ldx #2	jsr GoPos	ldx #37DrawLup1	lda #$20	;an inverse space character	jsr cout	dex	bne DrawLup1Frame	inc Ypos	ldy Ypos	ldx #2	jsr GoPos	lda #$20	jsr Cout	ldy Ypos	ldx #38	jsr GoPos	lda #$20	jsr Cout	dec DrawCnt	;until the count equals zero	bne Frame	ldy YPos	ldx #2	jsr GoPos	ldx #36DrawLup2	lda #$20	;an inverse space character	jsr cout	dex	bne DrawLup2	rts;; WAIT ROUTINE;B_WAIT	SECB_WAIT2	PHAB_WAIT3	SBC #1	BNE B_WAIT3	PLA	SBC #1	BNE B_WAIT2	RTS;	ENDIF	ENDIF******************************************       Find Server		******************************************FindServers		; 	jsr ClearWindow	;clear the window	GotoXY 3,5	;move the cursor	WriteCStr SelectServ ;draw the prompt to select a server	FrameRect FrameParms3 ;draw a rectangleStartNbp		; 	bit ZoneFlag	;is there zones?	bpl FS1	;if no zones, assume MyZone	GotoXY 3,3	;move the cursor	WriteCStr CurrZone	;String "Current Zone:"	ldx #ZoneName	;then print the zone name	ldy #>ZoneName	;	WritePointer	;	WriteCStr Prompt6	;the prompt says: "Esc: Change Zones"	bra FS2	;FS1	WriteCStr Prompt1	;the prompt says: "Esc: Quit"FS2		; 	SViewPort ListWindow ;set the view port to the list window	WriteChar ClrWind	;clear it	jsr DrawBox	;draw a temporary box	WriteChar Return	;next line	WriteCStr FSLookup	;Print "Looking for AFP File Servers"@dolookup	ATCall LkupPl	;do the NBP Lookup	bcc FS2C	;skip this check if no error	lda LkupPl+3	cmp #4	; NBP error?	bne @err	; no, skip the check	lda LkupPl+2	cmp #8	; was it "Too many NBP processes"?	beq @dolookup	; if so, try the call again@err	sec	; else it was some other errorFS2C	php	;save the status	jsr RestoreBox	;remove the box on the screen	SViewPort ListWindow ;restore the view port to the list window	plp	;check the carry for an error	bcc ChooseSvr	;if clear, chooser the server	lda LkupPl+3	;check to make sure	this was a NBP error	cmp #4	;	bne FS3	;if not, a system error occurred	lda LkupPl+2	;check to see if it was a user buffer full error	cmp #$04	;	beq ChooseSvr	;if it was, display what we gotFS3	jmp SysErr	;ChooseSvr	ldx MatchNum	;get the number for matches	bne GotSvrs	;if not zero, show the list	ldx #7	;if none, do an error message and let the	ldy #0	;user try again if he wants	jsr ErrorHandler	;	cmp #Return	;if esc was pressed return to the caller	bne cs1	;	jmp FS2	;try the lookup againcs1	rtsGotSvrs		; 	stx ArrayCnt	;set up the ListParm ArrayCnt	lda #<NBPBuffer	;initialize zero page for indexing into the buffer	sta StgPtr	;	lda #>NBPBuffer	;	sta StgPtr+1	;	lda #<ArrayBuff	;Arraybuff is where we will have a list of pointers	sta StgPtr2	;	sta StgArrayPtr	;set up the ListParm StgArrayPtr	lda #>ArrayBuff	;	sta StgPtr2+1	;	sta StgArrayPtr+1	;GetPointer	phx	;save the x register	clc	;add five to the NBP tuple	lda #5	;so that we are pointing to the string	adc StgPtr	;that is the name of the File Server	sta StgPtr	;	lda #0	;	adc StgPtr+1	;	sta StgPtr+1	;	lda StgPtr	;get the low byte of the pointer	ldy #0	;	sta (StgPtr2),y	;store it into the Array buffer	lda StgPtr+1	;get the high byte	iny	sta (StgPtr2),Y	lda #2	;add two to StgPtr2 so that it 	jsr IncStgPtr2	;points to the next available location	ldx #3	GetNxtPtr	PushWord StgPtr	;	_NextStr	;move StgPtr three strings to the end of this	PullWord StgPtr	dex	;tuple	bne GetNxtPtr	;	plx	;get the x register back which has the number of tupples	dex	;until x = 0	bne GetPointer	;do it again	bit ZoneFlag	;are there zones?	bmi GS1	;if so, always display the list	ldx MatchNum	;get the count	cpx #1	;is there only one item?	bne GS1	;if not, display the list	stx SelIndex	;otherwise, pretend that this one was selected	lda #$80	;update the skipflag	sta SkipFlag	;	lda #Return	;the routine above us looks for return	rts	;GS1		;;; 12-Jun-91 MSD: Sort the list of file servers!;	lda ArrayCnt	pha	; push number of entries	PushWord #ArrayBuff	; push address of list of pointers	_SortArray	; Go sort that puppy!;; End of 12-Jun-91 MSD change.;	stz SelXPos	;Set the X position to zero	stz SelYPos	;Set the Y position to zero	stz Increment	;Set the increment to zero	ldx #1	;select the first item in the list	stx SelIndex	;	ldx #$44	;set for fill mode and keyboard navigation	stx ListOptByte	;	ListHandler ListParms ;here is the list	rts	;return** save node number*SaveNode		; 	lda #0	;offset is equal to zero	pha	;	PushWord #FSName	;push the destination buffer	lda #<ArrayBuff	;set up zero page memory	sta StgPtr	;	lda #>ArrayBuff	;	sta StgPtr+1	;	lda SelIndex	;now get the new zone from the array buffer	dec a	;index - 1	asl a	;times 2	tay	;use the y register	lda (StgPtr),y	;get the low byte	sta StgPtr2	;save it 	iny	;and get the high byte	lda (StgPtr),y	;	sta StgPtr2+1	;please save the upper byte	Pushword StgPtr2	;push the values from StgPtr2	_MoveStr	lda StgPtr2	;StgPtr2 points to the string in the NBPBuffer	sec	;five bytes back is the network number an other	sbc #5	;information that we need	sta StgPtr2	;	lda StgPtr2+1	;do a 16 bit subtratcion	sbc #0	;	sta StgPtr2+1	;	ldy #0	lda (StgPtr2),y	;this is the network number first byte	sta LoginPl+4	sta GetSPStatus+8	iny	lda (StgPtr2),y	;this is the network number second byte	sta LoginPl+5	sta GetSPStatus+9	iny	lda (StgPtr2),y	sta GetSPStatus+10	sta LoginPl+6	;this is the Node number	iny	lda (StgPtr2),y	;This is the Socket	number	sta GetSPStatus+11	sta LoginPl+7****************************************** Do a GetSPStatus to find out	** what versions are	supported and if	** the Server supports Scrambled	** Passwords		******************************************	ATCall GetSPStatus	;do a ASP Status to find out the	bcc GetVersStg	;particulars about this server	jmp SPStatErr	;GetVersStg		;what versions does it support 	lda ReplyBuff+3	;add the offset to find the version	clc	;strings.  Returned in bytes 3 & 2	adc #<ReplyBuff	;high byte, low byte	sta StgPtr	;update the zero page pointers	lda ReplyBuff+2	;	adc #>ReplyBuff	;	sta StgPtr+1	;	ldy #0	;	lda (StgPtr),y	;get the count of the number of strings	tax	;to search	inc StgPtr	bne GVS1	inc StgPtr+1GVS1	lda #0	;set String compare	for case insensitive	pha	PushWord #LogonStr	;pointer to String 2	PushWord StgPtr	;push the pointer to String 1	_CompareStr	;Compare the strings	pla	beq VersFnd	;if found, this is our server	PushWord StgPtr	;try the next string in the list	_NextStr	PullWord StgPtr	;pull the result into StgPtr	dex	;if not at the end of the list	bne GVS1	;check again	ldx #8	;there was not a match	ldy #$80	;	jsr ErrorHandler	;Incompatibale Version of AFP	rtsVersFnd		; 	lda #0	;indicate that no error occured	rts	;we found the versionCheckUAM		;	stx StgPtr2	;save the argument that was passed	sty StgPtr2+1	;	clc	lda ReplyBuff+5	;get the offset to the UAM strings	adc #<ReplyBuff	;	sta StgPtr	;store it in string pointer	lda ReplyBuff+4	;this is the high byte of the offset	adc #>ReplyBuff	;	sta StgPtr+1	;update our zero page	ldy #0	;get the number of UAM's available	lda (StgPtr),y	;	tax	;into the x register for our counter	inc StgPtr	;add one to our zero page pointer	bne @UAM1	;	inc StgPtr+1	;@UAM1		; 	lda #0	;set String compare	for case insensitive	pha	PushWord StgPtr2	;	PushWord StgPtr	;push the pointer to String 1	_CompareStr	;Compare the strings	pla	beq @GotUAM	;if found, this is our server	PushWord StgPtr	;try the next string in the list from the server	_NextStr	;calculate the next string in the list	PullWord StgPtr	;pull the result into StgPtr	dex	bne @UAM1	sec	rts@GotUAM	clc	rts*IncStgPtr2		;this routine add 2 to the zero page pointer	clc	;StgPtr2 and updates that 	adc StgPtr2	sta StgPtr2	lda StgPtr2+1	adc #0	sta StgPtr2+1	rts****************************************** The user has requested that we logon	** to a server in a different zone,	** so let's go get a list of zones and   ** then let the user	choose one.	******************************************ChangeZone		; 	jsr ClearWindow	;clear the window	GotoXY 3,3	;move the cursor	WriteCStr CurrZone	;write the prompt "Current Zone:"	ldx #ZoneName	;print the zone name	ldy #>ZoneName	;	WritePointer	;	GotoXY 3,5	;move the cursor	WriteCStr ChoseZone	; prompt the user to choose a new zone	FrameRect FrameParms3 ;draw the box for the list window	WriteCStr Prompt9 	;prompt the approriate key strokes	SViewPort ListWindow ;set the view port to the listwindow	ATCall GetInfo	;first check to see	if the bridge is still here	lda ABridge	;if zero, the bridge is gone	sta BridgeNode	; 25-Jun-91 MSD.  Also changed BNE		; below to BRA.	bra CZ3	;go ahead and try the GetZoneList callCZ1	stz ZoneFlag	;indicate that there are no zones	lda #1	;set up the zone name back to myzone	sta ZoneName	;wildcard	lda #'*'	;	sta ZoneName+1	lda #Return	;load with return character to indicate	success	rts	;and return*** added 25-Nov-92 DALtoCZ1	jsr RemoveZoneMessage	jmp CZ1*** end 25-Nov-92CZ3	jsr DisplayZoneMessage  ;added 25-Nov-92 DAL	ATCall GetZoneList	bcc CZ4	;no error, build the list	lda GetZoneList+3	;check to see if it	was a ZIP error	cmp #6	bne toCZ1	;an error other than ZIP occurred	lda GetZoneList+2	;get the error	cmp #2	;is the error buffer overflow?	bne toCZ1	;if not, change back to my zone and leaveCZ4	lda #<NBPBuffer	;set up our zero page variables	sta StgPtr	;	lda #>NBPBuffer	;StgPtr points to the list of zones that have	sta StgPtr+1	;been returned by the server	lda #<ArrayBuff	;StgPtr2 is our pointer to the array buffer where we	sta StgPtr2	;will build an array of pointers to the strings	sta StgArrayPtr	;set up ListParms	lda #>ArrayBuff	;	sta StgPtr2+1	;	sta StgArrayPtr+1	;set up ListParms	lda ZoneCount	;get the number of zones	sta ArrayCnt	;set up ListParms	tax	;and into the x register for our counterCZ2	lda StgPtr	;get the low byte of the pointer		ldy #0	;	sta (StgPtr2),y	;store in into the array buffer	lda StgPtr+1	;get the high byte	iny	;	sta (StgPtr2),y	;store it into the next byte of the array buffer	lda #2	jsr IncStgPtr2	;add two to StgPtr2	PushWord StgPtr	;then low byte	_NextStr	;move StgPtr to the next string in the list	PullWord StgPtr	;update StgPtr	dex	;until x = 0	bne CZ2	;	lda ArrayCnt	;	pha	PushWord #ArrayBuff	_SortArray	jsr RemoveZoneMessage  ;added 25-Nov-92 DAL	lda ArrayCnt	pha	PushWord #ArrayBuff	PushWord #ZoneName	_FindItem	pla	sta SelIndex	;	stz SelXPos	;ListParm XPos = 0		stz SelYPos	;ListParm YPos = 0	stz Increment	;ListParm increment = 0	ldx #$44	;set for fill mode and keyboard navigation	stx ListOptByte	;	ListHandler ListParms ;get the user's selection	rts	;then return*** added 25-Nov-92 DAL -- display "Building Zone List..." boxDisplayZoneMessage	SViewPort ListWindow ;set the view port to the list window	WriteChar ClrWind	;clear it	jsr DrawBox	;draw a temporary box	WriteChar Return	;next line	WriteCStr BuildZL	;Print "Looking for AFP File Servers"	rtsRemoveZoneMessage	jsr RestoreBox	;remove the box on the screen	SViewPort ListWindow ;restore the view port to the list window	rts*** end 25-Nov-92TheNewZone	lda #0	;set up the command for zero offset	pha	;	PushWord #ZoneName	;Push the pointer to ZoneName (destination)	lda #<ArrayBuff	;set up zero page memory	sta StgPtr2	;	lda #>ArrayBuff	;	sta StgPtr2+1	;	lda SelIndex	;now get the new zone from the array buffer	dec a	;index - 1	asl a	;times 2	bcc @noinc	;MSD: carry in yo upper byte of offset?	inc StgPtr2+1	;MSD: yes, so point into upper part of array@noinc	tay	;use the y register	lda (StgPtr2),y	;get the low byte	pha	;save it 	iny	;and get the high byte	lda (StgPtr2),y	;	tax	;transfer the high byte into the x register	pla	;get the low byte into the A register 	phx	;push the high byte (source)	pha	;then the low byte (source)	_MoveStr	rts****************************************** Log On to the Server, But first we	** must move the Parameter list so that	** we will be able to Logon.	**		** Assumption made that Packets sent to	** the File Server will never be greater	** 256 bytes.		******************************************DoLogon	stz OtherSrvrFlg	;clear the another server flag	ldy #$12	;set the command byte of the Logon Packet	sty LogPckt	;	ldy #1	;the offset = 1	phy	;move the offset onto the stack		sty MovOffset	;save it for future calulations	PushWord #LogPckt	;push the destination	PushWord #LogonStr	;push the source	_MoveStr	;move the string	lda LogonStr	;get the string length	clc	;	adc MovOffset	;add the offset	inc a	;account for the string length	sta MovOffset	;update Move Offset	ATCall GetSPStatus	;call the Server for GetServerInfo	bcc DL1	;if no error, check UAMSPStatErr	lda GetSPStatus+2	;get the error byte	cmp #6	;Server not responding	bne DL2	;if server not responding it could have	ldy #$80	;been shutdown.  Go get another server	sty OtherSrvrFlg	;	ldx #4	;tell the user first	jmp DoLogErr	;DL2	jmp SysErr	;an error other than Server not respondingDL1		; 	bit AuthFlag	;test the guest flag	bpl UserAuth	;if not set, do user authentication	ldx #<Guest	;check to see if this server supports	ldy #>Guest	;	jsr CheckUAM	;	bcc GuestOk	;the string was found	lda #$16	;do a logon err	jsr LogErr3	;	rts	;then returnGuestOk		;now build the logon packet	lda MovOffset	;for logging on as a guest	pha	;push the offset	PushWord #LogPckt	;push the destination		PushWord #Guest	;push the source	_MoveStr	;move the string	lda Guest	;get the length of the guest string	clc	;add it to the current offset	adc MovOffset	inc a	;take into account for the string length	jmp CheckLogin	;there is no user or password for guestsUserAuth		;	stz UserAuthFlag	;initialize the user authtenticaion flag	ldx #<RanExch	;check to see if random exchange is supported	ldy #>RanExch	;	jsr CheckUAM	;see if the server has this string	bcc @UA1	;if not do a logon error message	lda #$80	;try clear text password	sta UserAuthFlag	;this is a flag used later	ldx #<ClrText	;check to see if random exchange is supported	ldy #>ClrText	;	jsr CheckUAM	;see if the server has this string	bcc @UA2	;if it does, logon with this UAM	ldx #9	;otherwise the user cant use this server	ldy #$80	;sorry Charlie!	jsr ErrorHandler	;	rts	@UA1	lda MovOffset	;for logging on using random exchange	pha	;push the offset	PushWord #LogPckt	;push the destination		PushWord #RanExch	;push the source	_MoveStr	;move the string	lda RanExch	;get the length of the user string	clc	;add it to the current offset	adc MovOffset	inc a	;take into account for the string length	sta MovOffset	;update move offset	bra @UA3	@UA2	lda MovOffset	;for logging on using clear text	pha	;push the offset	PushWord #LogPckt	;push the destination		PushWord #ClrText	;push the source	_MoveStr	;move the string	lda ClrText	;get the length of the user string	clc	;add it to the current offset	adc MovOffset	inc a	;take into account for the string length	sta MovOffset	;update move offset@UA3	pha	;push the offset	PushWord #LogPckt	;push the destination		PushWord #NameBuffer ;push the source	_MoveStr	;move the string	lda NameBuffer	;get the length of the user name string	clc	;add it to the current offset	adc MovOffset	inc a	;take into account for the string length	sta MovOffset	;update move offset		;	tax	;do we need to pad the buffer for the user	lsr a	;name?	bcc @NoPad	;not if there is no carry	stz LogPckt,x	;store a zero in the user buffer	inc MovOffset	;update move offset@NoPad	lda MovOffset	;get the count into the packet buffer	bit UserAuthFlag	;with user authentication method?	bpl CheckLogin	;go here with the packet length	ldy MovOffset	;get the offset into the buffer	ldx #8	;we will move eight bytes@UA4	lda PassBuffer,x	;from the password buffer 	sta LogPckt,y	;to the logon packet	iny	;next y	dex	;until x = 0	bne @UA4 	;	lda MovOffset	;get the length of the packet	clc	;add the eight bytes for the	adc #8	;clear text password	CheckLogin		; 	sta PakLen	;update the FPLogin parameter list	stz PakLen+1	;	stz LogErrCnt	;the error count down tickerLogRetry	;		IF (OSFlag = 128) or (OSFlag = 0) then	lda #$2b	;this is the old style login call	sta LoginPl+1	ATCall LoginPl	;do the login call	ENDIF		IF (OSFLAG = 192) or (OSFlag = 64) then	lda #$38	; FILogin2 call	sta LoginPl+1	lda #<FSName	;set up the parameter to the 	sta LoginPl+$19	;server name	lda #>FSName	;	sta LoginPl+$1a	;	lda #<ZoneName	;set up the parameter to the	sta LoginPl+$1d	;zonename	lda #>ZoneName	;	sta LoginPl+$1e	;	ATCall LoginPl	;do the newly defined login call for GS/OS	ENDIF	bcs LogErr	;if error, good luckLogonOk		; 	lda #0	;indicate to the calling routine success	rts	;LogErr		; 	inc LogErrCnt	;increment the error counter	lda LoginPl+2	;get the error resultLogonErr		; 	cmp #4	;was the error a ContLogin error?	bne LogErr1	;if not, check next error	jmp ContLogin	;otherwise, ContLoginLogErr1		; 	cmp #$13	;Already Logged on to File Server?	bne LogErr2	;if not, check next error	ldx MatchNum	;special case if there is only	cpx #1	;one server and no zones	bne LE1	;so that there is no two way branch	bit ZoneFlag	;what the hey	bmi LE1	;	ldy #$80	;there is one server and no zones	bra LE2	;make this an alertLE1	ldy #0LE2	ldx #12	jmp DoLogErrLogErr2		; 	cmp #$15	bne LogErr3	ldy #$80	ldx #3	;Unauthorized Password	bra DoLogErrLogErr3	cmp #$16	;Unauthorized User	bne LogErr4	ldy #$80	ldx #1	jmp DoLogErrLogErr4		; 	cmp #$17	;Server going down	bne LogErr5	ldy #$80	sty OtherSrvrFlg	ldx #17	bra DoLogErrLogErr5		; 	cmp #2	;Unable to open a server session	bne LogErr6	lda LogErrCnt	;AppleShare may not	be able to help us right now	cmp #$4	;before we decide that there are too many users	bge @1	jmp LogRetry	;we will retry 4 times@1	ldy #$80	;after 4 attempts tell them that there are	sty OtherSrvrFlg	;too many users, indicate another server	ldx #19	;Error message 19	bra DoLogErr	;display the message.LogErr6		; 	cmp #3	;Server not responding	bne LogErr7	ldy #$80	sty OtherSrvrFlg	ldx #4	bra DoLogErrLogErr7		; 	cmp #1	;The workstation has too many open sessions	bne UnkLogErr	ldy #$80	ldx #18	jsr ErrorHandler	jmp ByeByeUnkLogErr	jmp SysErrDoLogErr	jsr ErrorHandler	rtsContLogin		; 	lda LoginPl+$14	;get the session number	sta CLSess	;update the ContLogin session number	lda ReplyBuff	;get the Login ID	sta LogID	;	lda ReplyBuff+1	;	sta LogID+1	;update ContLogin parameter list	lda #<ReplyBuff+2	;set up the DES parameter list with the	sta DesParms+2	;key that was returned by	lda #>ReplyBuff+2	;the server	sta DesParms+3	;	lda #<DesLogRes	;tell the DES routine to put the Result here	sta DesParms+4	;	lda #>DesLogRes	;	sta DesParms+5	;	ldx #<DesParms	;call DES	ldy #>DesParms	;	jsr DES	;	ATCall ContLogPl	;then Call ContLogin	bcs ContLogErr	;if no error return to caller	jmp LogonOk	;ContLogErr	lda ContLogPl+2	;in case of error, get the error from our parms	jmp LogonErr	;and let LogonErr handle it** save session number*SaveSess		;               	lda LoginPl+$14	;get the session reference number	sta FIMountVol+$04	;update FIMountVol	sta GSSess	;update SPCommand	sta SPWrite+8	;update SPWrite	stz SPCommand+$F	;set the reply buffer length to	lda #2	;256 bytes	sta SPCommand+$10	;	lda #<ReplyBuff	;set the address of the command block	sta SPCommand+$11	;to the reply buffer	lda #>ReplyBuff	;	sta SPCommand+$12	;	lda #<GSPComm	;set up the SPCommand list for GetSrvrParms	sta SPCommand+$B	;to point to the one byte command #16	lda #>GSPComm	;	sta SPCommand+$C	;	lda #1	;the command is one byte in length	sta SPCommand+9	;	stz SPCommand+10	;	ATCall SPCommand	;issue the command	bcc GSok	;branch if no error	jmp SysErrGSok		; 	lda #<ReplyBuff	;set up the zero page pointer StgPtr for the 	sta StgPtr	;returned list of volume names	lda #>ReplyBuff	;	sta StgPtr+1	;	ldy #4	;the fourth byte is the number of volumes	lda (StgPtr),y	;get number of volumes returned	sta ArrayCnt	;save it in the ListParms variable	lda #5	;add five to the the zero page variable	clc	;to point to the first volume	adc StgPtr	;	sta StgPtr	;update zero page pointer StgPtr	lda #0	;	adc StgPtr+1	;and the high byte	sta StgPtr+1	;GVPoint	lda #<MySelArray	;set up zero page to the selection array	sta SelPtr	;	lda #>MySelArray	;	sta SelPtr+1	;	ldx ArrayCnt	;load the number of volumes into the x register	jsr CheckVols	IF OSFlag = 0 THEN	; ProDOS 8 app?		; don't care if no user volume mounted	ELSE	bit UMountFlag	;is a user volume already mounted?	bmi GVP1	;if so, we can continue	lda #$80	;for the first server accessed	sta OtherSrvrFlg	;it must have an associated user volume	rts	;so return, and look for another volume	ENDIFGVP1	lda ArrayCnt	cmp #1	;is there only one volume in the list?	bne GVolPoint	;no, so display the	list	tax	;get the selection byte	lda MySelArray,x	;and check to see if it is a user volume	cmp #$c0	;	bne GVolPoint	;if not, display the list	IF (OSFlag=128 or OSFlag=192) THEN	lda #0	; don't display the list if we're	rts	; booting over the network	ENDIFGVolPoint		; 	jsr ClearWindow	;clear the window	GotoXY 3,5	;move the cursor	WriteCStr SelectVol ;prompt: "Select the volumes you want to use:"	FrameRect FrameParms3 ;draw the list box	WriteCStr Prompt8	;prompt the user for the appropriate key storkes	SViewPort ListWindow ;set the view port for the list window	ldx ArrayCnt	;get the number of volumesMoveArray	lda MySelArray,x	;move the selection array to a copy	sta CompSelArray,x	;so we can compare changes later	dex	;	bne MoveArray	;	ldx ArrayCnt	;get the number of volumes again	lda #<ReplyBuff+6	;set up the zero page StgPtr to point to the	sta StgPtr	;volumes that have been return by the 	lda #>ReplyBuff+6	;file server.  The first string in the list is	sta StgPtr+1	;offset by 6 from the beginning	lda #<ArrayBuff	;set up zero page StgPtr2 to point to the Array	sta StgPtr2	;buffer where we will build an array of pointers	sta StgArrayPtr	;to the volume strings	lda #>ArrayBuff	;	sta StgPtr2+1	;	sta StgArrayPtr+1	;update the ListParm variables as wellGV3	ldy #0	;set the index to zero	lda StgPtr	;get the low byte of the pointer	sta (StgPtr2),y	;store it in the array buffer	iny	;next location		lda StgPtr+1	;get the high byte of the pointer	sta (StgPtr2),y	;update the array buffer	lda #2	jsr IncStgPtr2	;add two to StgPtr2	PushWord StgPtr	;push the parameters on the stack for	_NextStr	;make the call	PullWord StgPtr	;update StgPtr	inc StgPtr	;add one to StgPtr since there is a Password	bne GV1	;flag for each volume in the list	inc StgPtr+1	;GV1	dex	;until x = 0	bne GV3	;		lda #3	;set the x position to 3	sta SelXPos	;	stz SelYPos	;set the y position to zero	stz Increment	;set the increment to zero	ldx #1	;select the first item in the list	stx SelIndex	;	ldx #$84	;set for fill mode and Multiple Selection.	stx ListOptByte	;	ListHandler ListParms ;let the user select the volumes	cmp #Escape	;was escape pressed?	bne GV9	;if not, continue	lda #$c0	;indicate that an escape was pressed	rtsGV9		; 	ldx ArrayCnt	;get the number of volumes again	lda #<ArrayBuff	;set up our zero page variable StgPtr	sta StgPtr	;to point to the ArrayBuffer	lda #>ArrayBuff	;	sta StgPtr+1	;NxtSel	lda MySelArray,x	;check to see if changes were made for each	cmp CompSelArray,x	;volume	beq GV2	;this item has not been changed	jsr ItemSel	bcc GV5		stz MySelArray,x	;error: clear this item, so the volume wont appear mountedGV5	bit OtherSrvrFlg	;does the error require a new server?	bpl GV7	;if not, next item	lda #$80	;indicate to main that a new server is needed	rts	;GV7	bit NoMoreVols	;check to see if more volumes are allowed	bpl GV2	;if not, continue	jmp SaveSess	;start over with the current selectionGV2	dex	;until x = 0	bne NxtSel	;	bit MySel	;check to see if there were any changes	bmi GV4	;changes, so no message	ldx ArrayCntGV6	lda MySelArray,x	;Check to see that no volumes are	bmi GV4	;selected	dex	;if no volumes are mounted, log off the server	bne GV6LogMeOut		; 	lda LoginPl+$14	;force a logoff in case of error	sta FILogout+4	;	ATCall FILogout	;	lda #0	;return to main, task completed	rtsGV4	jsr CheckUserVol	; was a user volume mounted?	bmi @mounted	; yes, so no warning	ldy #$80	; no, warn about no user volume	ldx #29	; caution: no user volume	jsr ErrorHandler@mounted	lda #0	rtsItemSel		; 	phx	;save the x register	pha	;and the accumulator for use in this routine	txa	;this is the selected item	dec a	;item - 1	asl a	;multiply by 2	tay	;into the index register	lda (StgPtr),y	;get the low byte of the  volume string pointer	sta VolName	;update the FIMount parameter list	sta StgPtr2	;set up zero page for accessing the server volume list	iny	;next y index	lda (StgPtr),y	;get the high byte of the  volume string pointer	sta VolName+1	;update the FIMount parameter list	sta StgPtr2+1	;set up zero page for accessing the server volume list	sec	;subtract one from the zero page variable	lda StgPtr2	;to point to the password flag in the server volume	sbc #1	;list	sta StgPtr2	;	lda StgPtr2+1	;	sbc #0	;we will do it the old fashioned way, 16 bit	sta StgPtr2+1	;NS1	pla	;recover the original selection byte	bmi MntVol	;if the high bit is set, then mount the volume	stz MPassFlag	;otherwise, to unmount no password is required	bra PassNR	;go and unmount the volumeMntVol	lda (StgPtr2)	;check the password flag from the server		; (was (),y but we want first byte -MSD)	bmi PassAgain	;if the high bit is set, a password is required	lda #$80	;update the FIMount parameter list	sta MPassFlag	;	bra PassNR	;go mount the volumePassAgain	jsr GetPassWD	;go get the password from the user	bcs DoNxtSel	;if escape was pressed, forget itPassNR	jsr MountVol		bcc DoNxtSel	;if the carry is clear, no password error occured	bra PassAgain	;otherwise, try againDoNxtSel		; 	cmp #0	;if zero, then return to the caller	beq DS1	;	sec	;set the carry to indicate an error	bra DS2	;returnDS1	clcDS2	plx	;restore the x register	rts	;** mount volume*MountVol		; 	phx	;save x and y	phy	;	stz NoMoreVols	;initialize No More Volumes flagMV2	ATCall FIMountVol	;make the FIMount call	bcs MVErr	;if the carry is clear, download the icons	DoIcons	bit MPassFlag	bpl DI1	jsr AddIconsDI1	bit MPassFlag	;check bit 7 of the	Mount Flag	bpl DI2	;if unmounting, then do not check the access	jsr CheckAccess	;do we have the proper privileges for this volume?	bcc DI2	;if so, return to caller	lda MPassFlag	;get the current MPassFlag	pha	;save it	stz MPassFlag	;clear the PassFlag	for unmounting	ATCall FIMountVol	;unmount this volume	pla	;and restore the MPassFlag	sta MPassFlag	;	ldx #27	;Error Message "You	do not have Privileges for 	ldy #$80	;this Volume." This	is an alert.	jsr ErrorHandler	;do it	bra DoneItDI2	lda #0DoneIt	ply	plx	clc	rtsMVErr	lda FIMountVol+2	;check for errors	cmp #$11	;is the error Duplicate volume?	beq DupVolErr	cmp #$06	;msd: invalid session reference?	beq NoServErr	;msd: if so, assume	server shut down		;msd: used to assume invalid name	cmp #$07	;This Error code has two meanings	bne MV1	;server down, and bad password	bit MPassFlag	;check bit 6 of the	Mount Flag	bvc NoServErr	jmp PassErr	;if we are using a password assume it was badMV1	cmp #$05	;	bne TooManyVolErr	;last error, assume too many volumesInvalidNamErr	ldy #$80	ldx #2	;Invalid name error	jsr ErrorHandler	jmp DoneItNoServErr		; 	ldy #$80	sty OtherSrvrFlg	;no server error	ldx #4	jsr ErrorHandler	jmp DoneIt******************************************************************* Situation: This is a user volume that had been previously* been mounted as a regular volume when a user volume was * already mounted.  We are now back in Logon to add volumes, so* we will unmount and then remount this volume.******************************************************************DupVolErr	lda MPassFlag	;are we here to mount a user volume.	cmp #$81	;		bne DVE1	;if not, standard DupVolErr	jsr FindUserSess	;get the session number of the volume we want to mount	bcs DVE1	;if we cant find it, standard DupVolErr	lda GSSess	;compare this session to the session of the 	cmp OurVolSess	;volume	bne DVE1	;if not equal, standard DupVolErr	stz MPassFlag	;it is the same so unmount it	ATCall FIMountVol	;	lda #$81	;and then remount it as the User Volume	sta MPassFlag	;	jmp MV2	;DVE1	ldy #$80	;this stuff handles the standard	ldx #21	;duplicate volume error	jsr ErrorHandler	;	jmp DoneIt	;TooManyVolErr		; 	ldy #$80	;flag to indicate no more volumes	sty NoMoreVols	;	ldx #14	;and an error message to go along	jsr ErrorHandler	;	jmp DoneItPassErr		; 	ldy #$80	;the password was not correct	ldx #3	;	jsr ErrorHandler	;	sec	;set the carry for Item select	ply	;restore x and y	plx	rts	;returnFindUserSess		;StgPtr Variable points to the Volume we		;are trying to mount on this server	ldx SessNum	;The SessBuff is fresh from CheckUserVol	lda #<SessBuff	;reset the buffer to the network	sta StgPtr2	;volume list.	lda #>SessBuff	sta StgPtr2+1	ldy #0	;get the session number of this volumeFUS1	lda (StgPtr2),y	sta OurVolSess	;this is the returned result	lda #2	;move the variable StgPtr2 to point	jsr IncStgPtr2	;add two to point to the string	lda #0	pha	;push the compare flag	PushWord StgPtr2	;push String1	PushWord StgPtr	;push String1	_CompareStr	pla	;get the result	beq FUS2	;the volume matched, check session number	lda #30	;each volume to compare is 32 bytes apart	jsr IncStgPtr2 	;add 30 since we have already added	dex	;until the number of mounted volumes =	bne FUS1	;zero	sec	;user volume not found	rts	;FUS2	clc	;return with session number in OurVolSess	rts	********************************************************* CheckVols determines if a user volume	is mounted      * If not the User Volume is mounted.    *	                    * It then Updates the selection array to select all     * mounted volumes.* Inputs:*       Zero page variable StgPtr points to *       Buffer of volumes on server.*       Reg X = the	number of volumes in the Buffer* Outputs:*       UMountFlag = High bit set if User Volume is mounted*** 04-Jun-91  MSD	For the ProDOS 8 application, it allows*	a user volume to be not mounted.  If one*	is found, it is initially selected for*	mounting but may be deselected.********************************************************CheckVols		; 	stz SessBuff+1	; in case no volumes returned	stz SessBuff+2	phx	;save the number of	volumes returned by	the server	ldy #0	;clear out the selection index	tyaCV1	sta (SelPtr),y	; zero out MySelArray	iny	bne CV1	jsr CheckUserVol	cmp #0	;if the result is not zero, then a User	Volume	bne VolsMounted	;is already mounted** Mount a User Volume*	PushWord StgPtr	;save StgPtr on to the stack	ldy #0MUV2	lda (StgPtr),y	bit #1	;is the last bit set?	php	;save the results of this test	inc StgPtr	bne MUV5	inc StgPtr+1MUV5		; 	plp	;restore the processor flags	bne MUV1	;was bit zero set (i.e. user volume on this server)?	Pushword StgPtr	_NextStr	;calculate the next	string in the buffer	PullWord StgPtr	dex	;x still contains the number of volumes	bne MUV2	IF OSFlag=0 or OSFlag = 64 THEN		; application? (MSD 18-Jun-91)	bra MUV4	; yes, allow for no user volume mounted	ELSE	jmp SysErr	; other versions REQUIRE a user volume mounted	ENDIFMUV1	lda StgPtr	;move the volume string pointer	sta VolName	;to FIMountVol	lda StgPtr+1	sta VolName+1	lda #$81	;set it for a user volume and mount it	sta MPassFlag	jsr MountVol	cmp #0	;is the returned result zero?	beq MUV3	;if so mounting the	User Volume was successful	jsr LogMeOut	;log off of this server	bra MUV4MUV3		; 	lda #$80	sta UMountFlag	;update the User Volume mounted flag	jsr GetUserPfx	lda #<Prefix	;Set the User prefix path	sta FIBuffer	;	lda #>Prefix	;	sta FIBuffer+1	;	lda #$AA	;set the high bit of FIDirFlg	        	sta FIDirFlg	;to set the Name on	the card	ATCall FIUserPrefix	;set the prefix to the user path	stz FIDirFlgMUV4	Pullword StgPtr	;restore the zero page variable StgPtrVolsMounted		; 	plx	;restore the number	of volumes in x register	IF OSFlag=0 or OSFlag = 64 THEN		; for application, don't require user volume to be mounted	ELSE	bit UMountFlag	;If no user volume is mounted then this 	bmi VM9	;server cannot be used.	rts	ENDIFVM9	ATCall FIListSess	ldy #1	;y is the index for	the volume in the listCheckNext	phx	phy	lda #<SessBuff	;reset the buffer to the network	sta StgPtr2	;volume list.	lda #>SessBuff	sta StgPtr2+1	inc StgPtr	;String Pointer now	points to first volume	bne VM2	;update this pointer to point to the 	inc StgPtr+1	;volume name from the serverVM2		; 	ldx SessNum	;for each volume in	the network volume listVM4		; 	ldy #0	lda #$80	;this is the value to be stored in the 	sta SelFlag	;selection array	lda (StgPtr2),y	;get the session number for this volume	sta OurVolSess	iny	lda (StgPtr2),y	;get the slot/drive	of the volume	sta OurSlotDrive	;save the slot/drive of this volume	lda #2	;add two to the pointer	jsr IncStgPtr2	IF OSFlag=0 or OSFlag = 64 THEN		; application?		; yes, don't disable user volumes.	ELSE	lda OurSlotDrive	bit #1	;if bit 0 is set then, this is a 	beq VM8	;user volume.	lda #$c0	;set the selection array for selected	sta SelFlag	;and disabled	ENDIFVM8		; 	lda #0	 	pha	;set case insensitivity	PushWord StgPtr	;push the pointers to the strings	PushWord StgPtr2	;to be compared onto the stack	_CompareStr	pla	beq VM7	;the volume matched, check session numberVM3	dex	;check the next volume in the network list	beq VM5	;when x = 0, then all volumes have been	checked	lda #30	;next volume in the	network list 	jsr IncStgPtr2	;is 32 bytes away. Add thirty	    	bra VM4	;now compare this volumeVM5	ply	;set the selection array for not selected	lda (SelPtr),y	;and enabled	and #$3f	;by clearing bits 7	& 6	sta (SelPtr),y	bra VM6VM7		; ;volume is already mounted so mark inactive	lda OurVolSess	;test the session number	cmp GSSess	;	bne VM5	;if not this session, then no matchVM1	ply	lda (SelPtr),y	;update the selection array	ora SelFlag	sta (SelPtr),yVM6	PushWord StgPtr	_NextStr	;point to the next string	PullWord StgPtr	iny	plx	dex	;until all the volumes have been checked	beq VMDone	;	jmp CheckNext	;VMDone		; 	rtsCheckUserVol		;check to see if User Volume is mounted	phx	;save the registers	so they dont conflict	phy	;	stz UMountFlag	;clear the UserVol mounted flag	ATCall FIListSess	;get the list of current volumes	ldx SessNum	;number of volumes mounted	beq CUV2	;if no volumes are mounted, exit	ldy #1	lda #<SessBuff	;reset the buffer to the network	sta StgPtr2	;volume list.	lda #>SessBuff	sta StgPtr2+1CUV3	lda (StgPtr2),y	;get the slot drive	for this volume	bit #1	;if bit 0 is set then, a user volume is	mounted	beq CUV1	;	lda #$80	;	sta UMountFlag	;update the flag	bra CUV2CUV1		; 	dex	beq CUV2	lda #32	;next volume to compare is 32 bytes away	jsr IncStgPtr2	;add 32 to the zero page pointer StgPtr2	bra CUV3	;check the next oneCUV2		; 	ply	;restore the registers	plx	;	lda UMountFlag	;get the result	rts	;back to the calling routine	GetUserPfx		; 	jsr CheckUserVol	;build a prefix to the user directory	beq GUP7	;it will return with StgPtr2 pointing to the	lda #2	;ListSession data for this volume		jsr IncStgPtr2	;so add one to point to the zero page pointer	ldy #0GUP2	lda (StgPtr2),y	;get the length of the string	tay	;into the a register	inc a	;add two to the accumlator for the "/"'s	inc a	;	sta Prefix	;this is the new prefix length	lda #'/'	;get the backslash character	sta Prefix+1	;one goes here	sta Prefix+2,y	;the other here@TheLoop	lda (StgPtr2),y	;now move the rest of the string	sta Prefix+1,y	;into the prefix name buffer	dey	;until y = 0	bne @TheLoop	inc Prefix	;add one more for the string length	lda Prefix	;now point to the buffer behind the prefix	clc	;using zero page pointers	adc #<Prefix	;	sta StgPtr2	;	lda #>Prefix	;	adc #0	;our zero page pointer now points to the next	sta StgPtr2+1	;avialable location in the bufferGUP9	lda UserDir,y	;get the user directory string which is a C	beq GUP8	;type string	sta (StgPtr2),y	;into the prefix buffer	iny	;next y	bra GUP9	;exit is aboveGUP8		; 	tya	;y has how many bytes were moved	clc	;add it to the prefix length	adc Prefix	;	sta Prefix	;update the prefix length	clc	;	adc #<Prefix	;and move the zero page pointer again	sta StgPtr2	;	lda #>Prefix	;	adc #0	;msd: in case of wrap to next page	sta StgPtr2+1	;rbh: great job!!, mark	ldy #0	;now test if this is a guest or a user	bit AuthFlag	;	bmi DoGuestName	;if guest move the name "<Any User>"	ldx NameBuffer	;get the length of the user nameGUP3	lda NameBuffer+1,y	;get a byte from the name buffer	sta (StgPtr2),y	;move it to the prefix buffer	iny	;next index	dex	;until the end of the string	bne GUP3	;do it againGUP6	lda #'/'	;move a backslash into the prefix buffer	sta (StgPtr2),y	;	tya	;update the length of the prefix again	clc	;	adc Prefix	;	sta Prefix	;GUP7	rts	;and we are doneDoGuestname		; 	ldx GuestName	;get the length of the nameGUP5	lda GuestName+1,y	;get the byte	sta (StgPtr2),y	;move the name "<Any User>"	iny	;next index	dex	;until the end of the string	bne GUP5	;play it again, Mark	bra GUP6	;return to finish the jobDoGetInput		;Get the name and	password from the user	GotoXY 5,3	;clear the inverse from the first entry	WriteStr Entry1	;	GotoXY 0,10	;draw a line across	the center of the box	ReptChar TitLine	;	WriteCStr Prompt2	;at the bottom of the box, which keys are used	GotoXY 3,11	;Prompt -> "Enter your name and password:"	WriteCStr Prompt3	;	GotoXY 3,15	;Prompt -> "Password:"	WriteCStr PassField	;	GotoXY 3,13	;Prompt -> "Name:"	WriteCStr NameField	;	lda NameBuffer	;check the namebuffer	beq GetName	;if it is zero, then no name is written	GotoXY 9,13	;a name exists	WriteStr NameBuffer	;print the default name	jmp GN2	;go get the password firstGetName	stz OptionByte	;Option byte to indicate no encription	lda #NameLen	;maximum length for	a user name is 31 characters	sta MyLen	;	lda #<NameBuffer	;points to the buffer for default and output	sta InBuff	;	lda #>NameBuffer	;	sta InBuff+1	;	GotoXY 9,13	;move the cursor to	the position	Input MyParms	;give me your name	cmp #Escape	;if escape was pressed, punt this whole	idea	beq GN4	if OSFlag = 0 then	bit OptionByte	;check to see if input detected a modification	bvc GN2	;if overflow is clear, there was no change	jsr UpdateName	;update the user name it the ATINIT file	EndIFGN2	ldx #8	;maximum length for	the password is 8	stx MyLen	;@1	stz PassBuffer,x	;clear the password buffer with zeros	dex	bne @1	lda #<PassBuffer	;here is the buffer	to put the password	into	sta InBuff	;	lda #>PassBuffer	;	sta InBuff+1	;	stz PassBuffer	;no default passwords, always start fresh	lda #$80	;high bit of the option byte means encript display	sta OptionByte	;to the screen	GotoXY 13,15	;here is the cursor	location	Input MyParms	;go get the password	cmp #Return	;was it a return	beq GNDun	;if so, we are done	cmp #Escape	;an escape means that we can this adventure	bne GN3	;if not escape or return, it must be a TAB characterGN4		; 	sec	;indicate a punt	rts	;returnGN3	jmp GetName	;so go get the name	againGNDun		; 	clc	;indicate that we got the info! 	rtsGetPassWD		; 	lda #$c0	;set the the password field in FIMount	sta MPassFlag	;update the parameter list	jsr ClearWindow	;clear the window and not the title line	GotoXY 0,8	;move the cursor	ReptChar TitLine	;draw a line in the middle of the box	WriteCStr Prompt5	;give the appropriate key choices	GotoXY 3,9	;move the cursor	WriteCStr Prompt4	;prompt: "Enter the password for the volume:"	GotoXY 3,10	;now print the name of the volume	ldx VolName	;	ldy VolName+1	;	WritePointer	;	GotoXY 3,12	;prompt: "Password:"	WriteCStr PassField ;	ldx #8	;maximum length for	the password is 8	stx MyLen	;@1	stz PassBuffer,x	;clear the password buffer with zeros	dex	;	bne @1	;	lda #<PassBuffer	;update the parameter list for the input routine	sta InBuff	;	lda #>PassBuffer	;	sta InBuff+1		stz PassBuffer	;set the default length to zero	lda #$80	;set the option flag to invisiable characters	sta OptionByte	;VP2	GotoXY 13,12	;move the cursor to the input	Input MyParms	;get the password	cmp #Return	;check for return	bne VP1	;if not return, check for escape	clc	;return with the carry clear (No pun intended)	rts	;VP1	cmp #Escape	;was the character escape?	bne VP2	;	sec	rts****************************************** AddIcons downloads the Icons to the	** fileserver to support ProDOS.	**		** The routine checks for the Icon	** revision level and then determines if	** the icons needs to be updated.	******************************************AddIcons		; ;Download the ProDOS Icons	lda StgPtr	;save the zero page	string pointers	pha	lda StgPtr+1	pha	lda #12	;set up the Reply Buffer length	sta SPCommand+$F	stz SPCommand+$10	;of twelve (12)	lda #<FPReply	sta SPCommand+$11	;change the ReplyBuffer	lda #>FPReply	sta SPCommand+$12	;change the ReplyBuffer	lda #<OpenDT	;setup SP Command Paramters	sta SPCommand+11	lda #>OpenDT	sta SPCommand+12	lda #4	;Length of DTOpen	sta SPCommand+9	stz SPCommand+10	lda FIMountVol+10	;get the volume ID number	sta OpenDT+2	;store it into the OpenDT list	lda FIMountVol+11	;	sta OpenDT+3	;	ATCall SPCommand	;Open the DeskTop	bcc AI8	jmp AI3	;no need to close the desktopAI8	lda FPReply	;Get the DTRefNum	sta FPAddIcon+2	;and put it into the FPAddIcon	sta FPIconInfo+2	sta CloseDT+2	;also CloseDT	lda FPReply+1	;Parameter list	sta FPAddIcon+3	;	sta FPIconInfo+3	sta CloseDT+3	lda #<FPIconInfo	;setup SP Command Paramters	sta SPCommand+11	;to do the FPIconInfo call	lda #>FPIconInfo	;	sta SPCommand+12	;	lda #10	;Length of FPIconInfo	sta SPCommand+9	stz SPCommand+10	ATCall SPCommand	;make the FPIconInfo Call	lda SPCommand+$18	;check the result	beq AI6	;FPGetIcon Info call successful	cmp #$6c	;is it an item not found error?	beq UpdateIcon	jmp AI4	;another error occured, out of hereAI6		; ;compare the rev level with ours	sec	ldy #3AI7	lda FPReply,y	;get the Icon rev of the server	sbc FPAddIcon+14,y	;subtract ours from	the server rev	dey	bpl AI7	bcs AI4	;our icon rev is the same or lessUpDateIcon	ldx IconCount	;How many Icons are	there?	ldy #0	;get the Address of	the IconAI2	lda IconCount+1,y	;	sta StgPtr	;update a zero page	pointer	iny	;	lda IconCount+1,y	;	sta StgPtr+1	;high and low byte	phy	;save the Y register	ldy #3	;The first items in	the Icon recordAI1	lda (StgPtr),y	;is the file type	sta FPAddIcon+8,y	;move it to the FPAddIcon parameter	dey	;list	bpl AI1	;4 bytes in all	ply	;restore the y register	lda StgPtr	;Add four bytes to the exsisting pointer	clc	;	adc #4	;update the SPWrite	ParmList	sta SPWrite+$11	;	lda StgPtr+1	adc #0	;	sta SPWrite+$12	;high and low byte	ATCall SPWrite	bcs AI4	iny	;point to the next icon parmlist	dex	;for IconCount times	bne AI2	;AI4		; 	lda #4	;Length of DTClose	sta SPCommand+9	stz SPCommand+10	lda #<CloseDT	;setup SP Command Paramters	sta SPCommand+11	lda #>CloseDT	sta SPCommand+12	ATCall SPCommand	;close the DeskTopAI3		; 	pla	sta StgPtr+1	;restore the zero page string pointers	pla	sta StgPtr	rtsCheckAccess		; 	lda StgPtr	;save zero page pointers	pha	;onto the stack	lda StgPtr+1	;so that they can be restored	pha	;	lda VolName	;set up zero page to be used with the	sta StgPtr	;fetching the name of this volume	lda VolName+1	;because we have to	add a / in the name	sta StgPtr+1	;	ldy #0	lda (StgPtr),y	;get the length	tay	;into the y register	inc a	;add one to the name lentgh	sta AccessName	lda #'/'	sta AccessName+1CA2	lda (StgPtr),y	;now move the rest of the string	sta AccessName+1,y	;into AccessName	dey	bne CA2	pla	;now restore zero page	sta StgPtr+1	;back to original pointers	pla	;	sta StgPtr	;	ATCall FIAccess	lda FIAccess+5	;get the user summary byte	clc	;clear the carry to	indicate Access is ok	bne CA1	;if not zero, then access allowed	sec	;sec carry, summary	byte says Access deniedCA1	rtsErrorHandler		;               	phx	;preserve the value	in the x register	cpy #0	;if minus flag clear then this is an alert	bmi IsAlert	;you can only accept!	ldy #0	;if minus flag clear then this is a dialog IsAlert		; ;with two possible paths.	txa	asl a	tax	lda MessTbl,x	;get the low byte of pointer to the String	sta MessPtr	;into the Y register for a second	lda FilProcTbl,x	sta FilterProc	inx	;increment the pointer	lda MessTbl,x	;get the high byte of pointer to the String     	sta MessPtr+1	;	lda FilProcTbl,x	sta FilterProc+1	sty MessOptGoMessage	Message MessParms	plx	;restore the X register	rtsDrawBox		;               	lda #%01000000	sta MessOpt	stz FilterProc	stz FilterProc+1	Message MessParms	rtsRestoreBox		;               	lda #%00100000	sta MessOpt	stz FilterProc	stz FilterProc+1	Message MessParms	rtsProcFSName		; 	CenterStr FSName	rtsPathProc		; 	GetXY	ldx #2	lda #CD_GotoXY	jsr ConsDrvr	ldx #<OurPath	ldy #>OurPath	WritePointer	rtsPrefixProc			IF OSFlag = 0 or OSFlag = 128 or OSFlag = 192 then; 	GetXY	ldx #2	lda #CD_GotoXY	jsr ConsDrvr	ldx SetPrefix+1	ldy SetPrefix+2	WritePointer	EndIF	rtsVolProc		; 	GetXY	ldx #2	lda #CD_GotoXY	jsr ConsDrvr	ldx VolName	ldy VolName+1	WritePointer	rtsClearWindow		; 	lda #3	sta MainWindow+1	SViewPort MainWindow	WriteChar ClrWind	lda #1	sta MainWindow+1	SViewPort MainWindow	rtsCheckAT		;               	lda mli+2	;check to see if AppleTalk is installed	and #$f0	;clear off the low nibble	cmp #$c0	;is this pointing to a slot	bne @CA1	;Card is here but not installed	clc	;	rts@CA1	sec	rtsSysErr*** trigger the analyzer so we can see what the error was	lda #$aa	sta 0*** 	ldy #$80	ldx #0	jsr ErrorHandler	jsr LogMeOut	;just in case were logged on to a server	jmp ByeByeDrawLogOnScrn		; 	SViewPort SplashRect	WriteChar Return	CenterStr LogOnSplash1	WriteChar Return	CenterStr LogOnSplash2	WriteChar Return	CenterStr LogOnSplash3	rts**********************************************************************************	IF (OSFlag = 128) or (OSFlag = 0) or (OSFlag = 192) thenLoadAtinit		;should NEVER be called by P16 application	lda #$80	sta FINaming+5	ATCall FINaming	lda #<Prefix	sta SetPrefix+1	lda #>Prefix	sta SetPrefix+2	jsr mli	DC.B $c6	DC.W SetPrefix	bcc LAT1	jmp ATOpenErrLAT1	lda #<UserFName	;get the high byte of the pathname to open	sta Fopen+1	;store it in the Open parameter list	lda #>UserFName	;get the low byte of the pathname to open	sta Fopen+2	;store it in to the	paramter list	jsr mli	DC.B $c8	DC.W FOpen	bcc LAT2	jmp ATOpenErrLAT2	lda FOpen+5	sta FRead+1	lda #<ReplyBuff	sta DataBuf	lda #>ReplyBuff	sta DataBuf+1	lda #$ff	sta ReqCnt	sta ReqCnt+1	jsr mli	DC.B Read	DC.W FRead	bcc LAT3	jmp ATOpenErrLAT3		; 	jsr mli	DC.B $cc	DC.W FClose	lda TranCnt	clc	adc #<ReplyBuff	sta EOFPntr	lda TranCnt+1	adc #>ReplyBuff	sta EOFPntr+1	clcLAT4		;always exit thru	here to restore Naming mode	rtsATOpenErr	IF (OSFlag=128 or OSFlag=192) THEN	bra ATErr1	ENDIF	IF (OSFlag=0 or OSFlag=64) THEN	sec	bra LAT4	ENDIFATErr1	ldy #$80	ldx #15	jsr ErrorHandler	jmp ByeByeCheckMail		;should NEVER be called by P16 apps	lda #<Prefix	;Set the User prefix path	sta FIBuffer	;	lda #>Prefix	;	sta FIBuffer+1	;	ATCall FIUserPrefix	;set the prefix to the user path	jsr LoadAtinit	;set the user prefix and load in ATINIT	bcs NoMail	;if ATINIT is not configured, there is no mail	lda #<MailName	;set up the parameters for the Open call	sta Fopen+1	;	sta GetFInfoParm+1	lda #>MailName	;	sta Fopen+2	;	sta GetFInfoParm+2	jsr mli	;is it a directory?	DC.B GetFInfo	DC.W GetFInfoParm	bcs NoMail	lda GetFInfoParm+4	cmp #$0f	bne NoMail	;this is not a directory	jsr mli	;and open the directory "Mail" in the 	DC.B $c8	;user directory	DC.W FOpen	;	bcs NoMail	;there is no folder	called Mail	lda FOpen+5	;get the open Reference number	sta FRead+1	;into the Read Parameter list	lda #<ArrayBuff	;set up the Data Buffer	sta DataBuf	;	lda #>ArrayBuff	;	sta DataBuf+1	;	stz ReqCnt	;and a request count of 512	lda #1	;	sta ReqCnt+1	;	jsr mli	;and then read it in	DC.B $ca	;	DC.W FRead	;	bcs NoMail	;if the carry is set an error occurred		; ;	jsr mli	;close the file	DC.B $cc	;	DC.W FClose	;	lda ArrayBuff+$25	;this is the offset	for the number	bne GotMail	;of files in this directory	lda ArrayBuff+$26	;check both bytes for zero	beq NoMail	;if both are zero, then there is no mailGotMail	ldy #$80	;there is mail, display the message	ldx #20	;need to add message to list....	jsr ErrorHandler	;oh, yeah!NoMail		;job is done, no casualties	stz FINaming+5	;restore the naming	mode back to ProDOS	jsr mli	;	DC.B $42	DC.W FINaming	rts	EndIF		IF OSFlag = 0 thenCheckNetVol		; ;is this volume a	network volume?	jsr mli	;do the block read	DC.B ReadBlock	;ProDOS Command	DC.W RBParm	;our parameter list	cmp #$88	;did we get a network error?	beq CNL2	;if not then this is not a network volume	clc	;indicate that the volume is local 	rts	;and returnCNL2		; 	sec	;the volume is on the network	rts	;returnGetVolPfx		;this routine gets the volume prefix	jsr mli	;make the online call	DC.B $c5	;the Unitnum was stored here at launch time	DC.W OnLineParm	;	lda ReplyBuff	;get the byte that contains the volume length	and #$0f	;clear the high nibble	tay	;into the accumulator	inc a	;plus one	inc a	;plus two for dos "/"s	sta Prefix	;store the volume name length	lda #'/'	;put the backslashes into the name	sta Prefix+1	;one goes here	sta Prefix+2,y	;the other here at the end of the fileTheLoop2	lda ReplyBuff,y	;now move the bytes	    	sta Prefix+1,y	;from the reply buffer to the Prefix buffer	dey	;until all of them are moved	bne TheLoop2	;	rts	;GetUserName		; 	jsr CheckNetVol	;rbh: are we running on a network volume?	bcc @3	jsr GetNetName	;rbh: get the name from the server	bcc @2@1	stz NameBuffer	rts@2	tay	;save the accumulator, it has the low byte	lda #0	;to FPReply and x has the high byte	pha	;set the offset to zero	PushWord #NameBuffer;destination first	phx	;first the source high byte	phy	;then the source low byte	_MoveStr	;	rts@3		; 	jsr SetPath	jsr mli	DC.B $c6	DC.W SetPrefix	bcs @1	stx FOpen+1	sty FOpen+2	jsr mli	DC.B Open	;	DC.W FOpen	;	bcs @1	;open failed, punt	lda FOpen+5	;get the reference Number	sta FRead+1	;store the reference numbers for other calls	sta GetEofParm+1	;	sta SetMarkParm+1	;	sta FClose+1	;	jsr mli	;get the end of file 	DC.B GetEof	;	DC.W GetEofParm	;	bcs @1	;if an error occurred, there will be no	update to the username	sec	;set the carry for subtraction	lda GetEofParm+2	;get the LSB of the	EOF	sbc #<NameOffset	;subtract the name offset	sta SetMarkParm+2	;store it in the set mark parameter list	lda GetEofParm+3	;	sbc #>NameOffset	;subtract the upper	byte	sta SetMarkParm+3	;	lda GetEofParm+4	;and the high byte	sbc #0	;	sta SetMarkParm+4	;we now have the mark in the file	jsr mli	;	DC.B SetMark	;	DC.W SetMarkParm	;	lda #33	sta FRead+4	stz FRead+5	lda #<NameBuffer	sta FRead+2	lda #>NameBuffer	sta FRead+3	jsr mli	DC.B Read	DC.W FRead	bcc @4	jmp @1@4		; 	jsr mli	DC.B Close	DC.W FClose	rts	;ChangePass		; 	GotoXY 5,7	WriteStr Entry3	GotoXY 0,10	ReptChar TitLine	WriteCStr Prompt2	;which keys can be used	GotoXY 3,11	WriteCStr Prompt7	;display instructions to user	GotoXY 3,13	WriteCStr NewPassword ;prompt - "New Password:"CP3	stz NewPasswrd	stz OptionByte	lda #08	sta MyLen	lda #<NewPasswrd	sta InBuff	lda #>NewPasswrd	sta InBuff+1	GotoXY 17,13	Input MyParms	cmp #Escape	bne ChangeIt	sec	rtsChangeIt		; 	lda LoginPl+$14	;get the current session number	sta GSSess	;this is in the middle of SPCommand	sta FILogout+4	;same session to logout	ldx NewPassWrd	;get the length of the password	inx	;Point to the first	character in string	lda #8	;subtract 8     	sec	;	sbc NewPassWrd	;from the length of	the new password	beq CP1	;if new password is	8, no padding is needed	tay	;x register has how	many zeros to placeCPadZeros	stz NewPassWrd,x	;clear buffer until	x = 0	inx	;	dey	;	bne CPadZeros	;CP1		; 	lda #<NewPasswrd	;ok, now encript the new password	sta DesParms+2	;	lda #>NewPasswrd	;	sta DesParms+3	;this time the result goes here	lda #<FPChangePass2	;	sta DesParms+4	;	lda #>FPChangePass2	;	sta DesParms+5	;	ldx #<DesParms	ldy #>DesParms	jsr DES	lda #<PassBuffer+1	;setup the parameter list to scramble the	sta DesParms+2	;old password with the new one	lda #>PassBuffer+1	sta DesParms+3	;	lda #<FPChangePass1	;place the DES result here	sta DesParms+4	;	lda #>FPChangePass1	;	sta DesParms+5	;	ldx #<DesParms	;and then call the Des Encription routine	ldy #>DesParms	jsr DES	lda #12	;set up the Reply Buffer length	sta SPCommand+$F	;none is really needed for this call	stz SPCommand+$10	;of twelve (12)	lda #<FPReply	;here is the reply buffer	sta SPCommand+$11	;change the ReplyBuffer	lda #>FPReply	;	sta SPCommand+$12	;change the ReplyBuffer	lda #<FPChangePass	;setup SP Command Paramters	sta SPCommand+11	;tell FPCommand where the parameters are	lda #>FPChangePass	;	sta SPCommand+12	lda #36	;Length of FPChangePass	sta SPCommand+9	stz SPCommand+10	ATCall SPCommand	;Change the password	bcc CPDunCPDun	ATCall FILogout	;and then logout from the server	clc	;indicate that Return was pressed! 	rtsGetNetName		; 	ATCall FIListSess	ldx SessNum	bne GNN3	sec	rtsGNN3	lda #<SessBuff	sta StgPtr2	lda #>SessBuff	sta StgPtr2+1	ldy #1GNN1	lda (StgPtr2),y	bit #$01	bne GNN2	lda #32	;next volume to compare is 32 bytes away	jsr IncStgPtr2	dex	bne GNN1	sec	;we should never get here but just in case..	rts	;GNN2		; 	ldy #0	;get the Session reference number	lda (StgPtr2),y	;	sta GSSess	;	lda #33	;set up the Reply Buffer length	sta SPCommand+$F	;none is really needed for this call	stz SPCommand+$10	;of twelve (12)	lda #<FPReply	;here is the reply buffer	sta SPCommand+$11	;change the ReplyBuffer	lda #>FPReply	;	sta SPCommand+$12	;change the ReplyBuffer	lda #<FPGetUserInfo	;setup SP Command Paramters	sta SPCommand+11	;tell FPCommand where the parameters are	lda #>FPGetUserInfo	;	sta SPCommand+12	lda #8	;Length of FPGetUserInfo	sta SPCommand+9	stz SPCommand+10	ATCall SPCommand	;Get my UserID	ldy #2	;move the ID to FPMapIDNxtIDByte	lda FPReply,y	;User IDs are four bytes        	sta FPMapID,y	;move them into FPMapID	iny	;	cpy #6	;when Y = 6, we have move four bytes	bne NxtIDByte	;fall thru when done	lda #<FPMapID	;setup SP Command Paramters	sta SPCommand+11	;tell FPCommand where the parameters are	lda #>FPMapID	;	sta SPCommand+12	lda #6	;Length of FPMapID	sta SPCommand+9	stz SPCommand+10	ATCall SPCommand	;Get my name from the ID	lda #<FPReply	ldx #>FPReply	clc	rtsUpdateName		; 	jsr CheckNetVol	;no auto username for now	bcc UN2	;if this is a network volume, it does notUN6	rts	;need to be updatedUN2	jsr SetPath	;set the path to the ATINIT File	phx	phy	lda #<Prefix	sta SetPrefix+1	lda #>Prefix	sta SetPrefix+2	jsr mli	DC.B $c6	DC.W SetPrefix	bcc UN5	ply	plx	clc	;it failed, but who	cares	rts	;open failed, puntUN5	pla	;get the pointer to	the patnname	sta FOpen+2	;update the Open parameter list	pla	;and the low byte	    	sta FOpen+1	;	jsr mli	;open the file	DC.B Open	DC.W FOpen	bcc UN1	;if the carry is clear, continue	clc	;an error occurred	rts	;return as if there	was no user nameUN1	lda FOpen+5	;get the reference Number	sta FWrite+1	;store the reference numbers for other calls	sta GetEofParm+1	;	sta SetMarkParm+1	;	sta FlushParm+1	sta FClose+1	lda LastDev	;msd: Get current device	sta UnitNum	;msd: and use it for Online call	jsr mli	;get the end of file 	DC.B GetEof	DC.W GetEofParm	bcs UN4	;if an error occurred, there will be no	update to the username	sec	;set the carry for subtraction	lda GetEofParm+2	;get the LSB of the	EOF	sbc #<NameOffset	;subtract the name offset	sta SetMarkParm+2	;store it in the set mark parameter list	lda GetEofParm+3	;	sbc #>NameOffset	;subtract the upper	byte	sta SetMarkParm+3	;	lda GetEofParm+4	;and the high byte	sbc #0	;	sta SetMarkParm+4	;we now have the mark in the fileUN3	jsr mli	;msd: Force ProDOS to find out what	dc.b Online	;msd: disk is in the drive.	dc.w OnlineParm	;msd: (Detect disk switched)	bcs UN7	;msd: Check for possible errors	jsr mli	DC.B SetMark	DC.W SetMarkParm	bcs UN4	;if an error occurs, no update	jsr mli	;all is still well,	write the name out to the ATINIT file	DC.B Write	DC.W FWrite	bcs UN8	jsr mli	;this is a special fix for the UniDisk 3.5	DC.B Flush	;which does not know when it writes to a file	DC.W FlushParm	;that the disk is write protected	bcc UN4UN7	cmp #$2f	; Device offline ->	ask for volume	beq UN9	cmp #$2E	;msd: Disk switched	-> ask for volume	beq UN9UN8	cmp #$2b	;any error but write protect (2b) is undefined	bne UN4	;UN9	ldy #$80	;alert -> Please write enable this volume:	ldx #28	jsr ErrorHandler	bra UN3UN4		; 	jsr mli	;close the file	DC.B Close	;	DC.W FClose	;	rts	;the name is updatedSetPath		; 	jsr GetVolPfx	;rbh: build a prefix for the volume name	sec	;rbh: CHECK TO SEE IF WE'RE ON A IIGS	jsr CheckMach	bcs P8Disk	;rbh: Load ATINIT from P8 disk;	LONGA ON	;rbh: we are an Apple //gs	LDA p16flag	;rbh: GET FLAG AT $E100BD	LONGA OFF	;rbh: are we running under prodos 16?;	BEQ P8Disk	;rbh: NOT PRODOS 16P16Disk		; 	ldx #<P16FName	ldy #>P16FName	bra theNameP8Disk		; 	ldx #<P8FName	ldy #>P8FNametheName		; 	rts	ENDIF;------------------------------------------;; Console Parms;;------------------------------------------MyParms		; OptionByte	DC.B $00	;option ByteMyLen	DS.B 1	;maximum input lengthInBuff	DS.B 2	;Buffer for input/output	DC.W MyTermList	;Termination CharactersMyTermList		; 	DC.B $03	DC.B Escape	DC.B TabHB	DC.B CrHB	;3 characters Esc, Tab and ReturnListParms		; SelXPos	DS.B 1SelYPos	DS.B 1Increment	DS.B 1ArrayCnt	DS.B 1StgArrayPtr	DS.B 2SelArray	DC.W MySelArraySelIndex	DS.B 1ListOptByte	DS.B 1InitParm	DC.B $80TitLine		; 	DC.W ULChars	DC.W 5ULChars		; 	DC.B MTON	DC.B ReptCharLinCnt	DC.B 50	DC.B 'L'	;top of the window underline character	DC.B MTOFFMainWindow	DC.B 15	DC.B 1	DC.B 64	DC.B 20FrameParms1		; Point1	DC.B 15	;x1	DC.B 00	;y1Point2	DC.B 65	;x2	DC.B 20	;y2WaitStr		; 	DC.B $02	;number of characters	DC.B WaitChar	;Control Character to indicate this is a wait	DC.B $ff	;this is how long to waitSplashRect		; 	DC.B 0	;x1	DC.B 9	;y1	DC.B 79	;x2	DC.B 15	;y2FrameParms3		; 	DC.B 5	;x1	DC.B 6	;y1 viewport+1	DC.B 45	;x2 viewport-1	DC.B 14	;y2ListWindow	DC.B 20	DC.B 8	DC.B 59	DC.B 15SaveArea	DC.B 9	DC.B 9	DC.B 71	DC.B 16Title	DC.B '  '	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'A'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B ' File Server Log On V1.5   '	DC.B Inv	DC.B CLEOL	DC.B Norm	DC.B CR	DC.B $00	;end of C StringCheckMark		; 	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'D'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B $00StrArray	DC.W Entry1	DC.W Entry2	DC.W Entry3Prompt1		; 	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 1	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Select:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'K J'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 20	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Cancel: Esc'	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 40	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Accept:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'M'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B $00Prompt2	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 1	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Change: Tab'	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 20	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Cancel: Esc'	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 40	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Accept:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'M'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B $00Prompt3	DC.B 'Enter your name and password:'	DC.B $00Prompt4	DC.B 'Enter the password for the volume'	DC.B $00Prompt5	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 1	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Cancel: Esc'	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 40	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Accept:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'M'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B $00Prompt6		; 	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 1	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Select:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'K J'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 15	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Change zones: Esc'	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 40	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Accept:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'M'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B $00Prompt7	DC.B 'Enter your old and new password:'	DC.B $00Prompt8		; 	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 1	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Select:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'K J H U'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 20	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Quit: Esc'	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 40	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Accept:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'M'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B $00Prompt9	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 1	DC.B 19	DC.B CLEOL	DC.B 'Select:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'K J'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 20	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Quit: Esc'	DC.B CPOS	DC.B 40	DC.B 19	DC.B 'Accept:'	DC.B MTON	DC.B 'M'	DC.B MTOFF	DC.B $00;------------------------------------------;; Message Variables;;------------------------------------------MessParmsMessOpt	DS.B 1MessPtr	DS.B 2FilterProc	DC.B $00,$00Rect		; 	DC.B 10	;x1	DC.B 9	;y1	DC.B 70	;x2	DC.B 15	;y2WindBuff	DC.W WindowBuffMessageWind	DC.B 10	DC.B 10	DC.B 69	DC.B 15Mess0		;               	DC.B (Mess0End-Mess0)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  An unknown system error has occurred.'	DC.B Return;;; Well, this will be a pain to get the error number stored here in all cases.;*** added 25-Nov-92 DAL;	DC.B '  (Error $';theErrorCode	DC.B 'xxxx)';	DC.B Return;*** end 25-Nov-92Mess0End		; Mess1		;               	DC.B (Mess1End-Mess1)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  Unknown user or login is disabled.  Please retype'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  the name or contact the network administrator.'Mess1End		; Mess2		;               	DC.B (Mess2End-Mess2)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' This volume does not have a proper ProDOS'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' pathname and cannot be used:'	DC.B ReturnMess2End		; Mess3		;               	DC.B (Mess3End-Mess3)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Sorry, your password is incorrect.'	DC.B Return	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Please reenter it.'Mess3End		; Mess4		;               	DC.B (Mess4End-Mess4)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  The server is not responding.'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  You cannot connect to it.'Mess4End		; Mess5		;               	DC.B (Mess5End-Mess5)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' This startup path was not found:'	DC.B ReturnMess5End		; Mess6		;               	DC.B (Mess6End-Mess6)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' An error occurred launching the startup path:'	DC.B ReturnMess6End		; Mess7		;               	DC.B (Mess7End-Mess7)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '       No servers were found.'	DC.B Return	DC.B Return	DC.B '       Press Return to try again.'Mess7End		; Mess8		;               	DC.B (Mess8End-Mess8)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  This file server uses an incompatible version'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  of the AFP protocol.  You cannot connect to it.'Mess8End		; Mess9		;               	DC.B (Mess9End-Mess9)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  This file server does not use a recognizable '	DC.B Return	DC.B '  logon sequence.  You cannot connect to it.'Mess9End		; Mess10		;               	DC.B (Mess10End-Mess10)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  The attempted connection to the server'	DC.B $27	DC.B 's'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  volume has failed.'Mess10End		; Mess11		;               	DC.B (Mess11End-Mess11)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' An error occurred setting the startup prefix:'	DC.B ReturnMess11End		; Mess12		;               	DC.B (Mess12End-Mess12)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  You are already logged on to the file server:'	DC.B Return	DC.B ReturnMess12End		; Mess13		;               	DC.B (Mess13End-Mess13)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  You have not marked any volumes.'Mess13End		; Mess14		;               	DC.B (Mess14End-Mess14)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  You have too many volumes in use.  To add '	DC.B Return	DC.B '  another you must first unmark one or more volumes.'	DC.B ReturnMess14End		; Mess15		;               	DC.B (Mess15End-Mess15)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  Your startup configuration has not been set up'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  properly. Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B ReturnMess15End		; Mess16		;               	DC.B (Mess16End-Mess16)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  AppleTalk must be installed to run this program.'Mess16End		; Mess17		;               	DC.B (Mess17End-Mess17)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  The server is closing down.  Try again later.'	DC.B ReturnMess17End		; Mess18		;               	DC.B (Mess18End-Mess18)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  You have reached the limit of the number of'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  file servers you can log on to at one time.'Mess18End		; Mess19		;               	DC.B (Mess19End-Mess19)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  This file server will not allow any additional'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  users to logon.  Try again later.'Mess19End		; Mess20		;               	DC.B (Mess20End-Mess20)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  You have mail waiting for you.'Mess20End		; Mess21		;               	DC.B (Mess21End-Mess21)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' This volume name already exists and cannot be used:'	DC.B ReturnMess21End		; Mess22		;               	DC.B (Mess22End-Mess22)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' To connect to this server, this volume must be'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' a vaild ProDOS name:'	DC.B ReturnMess22End		; Mess23		;               	DC.B (Mess23End-Mess23)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' An access error occurred launching the startup path:'	DC.B ReturnMess23End		; Mess24		;               	DC.B (Mess24End-Mess24)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' This path does not contain a ProDOS 8 startup application:'	DC.B ReturnMess24End		; Mess25		;               	DC.B (Mess25End-Mess25)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B ' Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B ' This path does not contain a ProDOS 16 startup application:'Mess25End		; Mess26		;               	DC.B (Mess26End-Mess26)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  Cancel to select additional volumes.'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  The volume with the startup application was not found:'	DC.B ReturnMess26End		; Mess27		;               	DC.B (Mess27End-Mess27)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  Contact the network administrator.'	DC.B Return	DC.B '  You do not have privileges to use this volume:'	DC.B ReturnMess27End		; Mess28		;               	DC.B (Mess28End-Mess28)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  Please write enable this volume:'	DC.B ReturnMess28End		; 	IF OSFlag = 0 THENMess29		;               	DC.B (Mess29End-Mess29)-1	DC.B Return	DC.B '  Caution: No user volume is mounted.'	dc.b Return	dc.b '  Some applications may fail.'Mess29End	ENDIF	MessTbl	DC.W Mess0	DC.W Mess1	DC.W Mess2	DC.W Mess3	DC.W Mess4	DC.W Mess5	DC.W Mess6	DC.W Mess7	DC.W Mess8	DC.W Mess9	DC.W Mess10	DC.W Mess11	DC.W Mess12	DC.W Mess13	DC.W Mess14	DC.W Mess15	DC.W Mess16	DC.W Mess17	DC.W Mess18	DC.W Mess19	DC.W Mess20	DC.W Mess21	DC.W Mess22	DC.W Mess23	DC.W Mess24	DC.W Mess25	DC.W Mess26	DC.W Mess27	DC.W Mess28	IF OSFlag = 0 THEN	dc.w Mess29	ENDIFFilProcTbl	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W VolProc	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W PathProc	DC.W PathProc	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W PrefixProc	DC.W ProcFSName	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W Null	DC.W VolProc	DC.W VolProc	DC.W PathProc	DC.W PathProc	DC.W PathProc	DC.W PathProc	DC.W VolProc	DC.W PrefixProc	IF OSFlag = 0 THEN	dc.w Null	; message 29	ENDIF;------------------------------------------;; AppleTalk Parameter Lists;;------------------------------------------LkupPl		; 	DC.B $00	;sync flag	DC.B $10	;command	DC.W 0	;result code	DC.L 0	;completion routine	pointer	DC.L server	;server name	DC.B 4	;retry interval	DC.B 10	;retry count	DC.W 0	;reserved	DC.W NBPBuffLen	;buffer length	DC.L NBPBuffer	;buffer address	DC.B $7F	;max matchesMatchNum	DC.B $02	;act matches** login parameter list*LoginPl		; 	DC.B $00	;sync flag	DC.B $2B	; FILogin command	DC.W 0	;result code	DC.W 0	;network	DC.B $00	;node	DC.B $00	;socketPakLen	DS.B 2	;length of command	DC.L logpckt	;address of command	packet	DC.W 0512	;length of reply buffer	DC.L replybuff	;address of reply buffer	DC.B $00	;session	DC.L 0	;attention routine	DC.L replybuff	;address of server name, gets modified before call	DC.L replybuff	;address of zone name, use replybuff to set up bank	dc.w AFPVersion	;for now, AFPVersion 2.0**Continue Login*ContLogPl		; 	DC.B $00	;sync flag	DC.B $2c	;command	DC.W 0	;result codeCLSess	DC.B $00	;session	DC.W 12	;length of command	DC.L ContLogPkt	DC.W 0512	;length of reply buffer	DC.L replybuff** GetSrvParms*SPCommand		; 	DC.B $00	;byte - sync flag	DC.B $20	;byte - ASP command	DC.W 0	;word - Result	DC.L 0	;long - Completion Routine PtrGSSess	DS.B 1	;byte - Session Number	DC.W 01	;word - Length of command buffer	DC.L GSPComm	;long - Address of command packet	DC.W 12	;word - Length of Reply Buffer	DC.L FPReply	;long - reply buffer pointer	DS.B 4	;long - command result	DS.B 2	;word - Reply LengthGSPComm	DC.B $10OpenDT	DC.B 48	DC.B $00	DS.B 2CloseDT	DC.B 49	DC.B $00	DS.B 2GetSPStatus		; 	DC.B $00	;sync flag	DC.B $1d	;command	DC.W 0	;result code	DC.L 0	;Completion Routine	DC.W 0	;network	DC.B $00	;node	DC.B $00	;socketStatLen	DC.W 512	;Max length of packet	DC.L ReplyBuff	;pointer to buffer	DC.W 0	;length of status dataSPWrite		; 	DC.B $00	DC.B $21	DC.W 0	DC.L 0	DS.B 1	DC.W 20	;command buffer length AddIcon	DC.L FPAddIcon	;command buffer pointer	DC.W 256	;write buffer length	DC.L SysIcon	;write buffer pointer	DC.W 12	;reply buffer length	DC.L FPReply	;reply buffer pointer	DS.B 4	;command result	DS.B 2	;length written	DS.B 2	;reply lengthFPAddIcon		; 	DC.B 192	DC.B $00	;reserved	DS.B 2	;DeskTop reference number	DC.B 'pdos'	DS.B 4	;File Type	DC.B $01	;IconType	DC.B $00	;reserved	DC.B '10B9'	;IconTag	DC.B $01,$00	;IconSizeFPIconInfo		; 	DC.B 52	DC.B $00	;reserved	DS.B 2	;DeskTop reference number	DC.B 'pdos'	DC.B $00,$01	;Icon IndexFPGetUserInfo		; 	DC.B $25	;FPUserInfo command	DC.B $01	;this user	DS.B 4	;UserID gets returned here	DC.B $00,$01	;bit map to indicate UserIDFPMapID		; 	DC.B $15	;FPMapID command	DC.B $01	;function byte 1 = map user ID to User Name	DS.B 4	;UserID to be mappedFPReply	DS.B 33** mount volume*FIMountVol		; 	DC.B $00	;byte - sync flag	DC.B $2e	;byte - command	DC.W 0	;word - result code	DC.B $00	;byte - session reference numberMPassFlag	DC.B $c0	;byte - password flagVolName	DC.L *	;long - volume name	pointer	DS.B 2	;word - volume ID	DC.B $cc	;byte - slot/drive	DC.L passbuffer+1FIUserPrefix		; 	DC.B $00	;byte - sync flag	DC.B $2a	;byte - command	DC.W 0	;word - result codeFIDirFlg	DC.B $00	;byte - direction flagFIBuffer	DC.L ReplyBuff	;long - pointer to bufferFILogout		; 	DC.B $00	DC.B $2d	DC.W 0	DS.B 1FIListSess		; 	DC.B $00	DC.B $2f	DC.W 0	DC.W 1024	DC.L SessBuffSessNum	DS.B 1GetInfo		; 	DC.B $00	DC.B $02	DS.B 2	DS.B 4	DS.B 2ABridge	DS.B 1	DS.B 1	DS.B 2	DS.B 1GetZoneList		; 	DC.B $00	DC.B $1b	DS.B 2	DC.L 0	DC.W NBPBuffLen	DC.L NBPBufferBridgeNode	DS.B 1StartIndex	DC.W 1	DC.B $04	DC.B $04ZoneCount	DS.B 1	DS.B 4;; 09-Jul-91 MSD: Changed retry count and interval;GetMyZone		; 	DC.B $00	;byte - sync flag	DC.B $1a	;byte - GetMyZone command	DC.W 0	;word - Result	DC.L 0	;long - Completion Routine Ptr	DC.L ReplyBuff	;long - Buffer Pointer	DC.B $04	;byte - Retry Interval	DC.B $04	;byte - Retry Count	DS.B 4	;long - ReservedFINaming		; 	DC.B $00	DC.B $33	DC.W 0	DC.B $80	DC.B $80FIAccess		; 	DC.B $00	;byte - sync flag	DC.B $32	;byte - FIAccess command	DC.W 0	;word - Result <-	DC.B $00	;byte - Direction Flag ->	DC.L 0	;long - Access Rights <->	DC.L AccessName	;long - pointer to volume string ->	DC.L 0	;long - Creator name pointer <->	DC.L 0	;long - Group name pointer <->Boot		; 	DC.B $00	DC.B $06	DC.W 0RegstrName	DC.B $00	DC.B $0e	DC.W 0	DC.L 0	DC.L ArrayBuff	DC.B $04	DC.B $04	DC.W 0RegSocket	DC.B $04	DC.B $00ContLogPkt		; 	DC.B $13	DC.B $00LogID	DS.B 2DesLogRes	DS.B 8FPChangePass		; 	DC.B $24	;FPChangePass Command	DC.B $00	str 'Randum Exchange'	DC.B $00	;null PadFPChangePass1	DS.B 8FPChangePass2	DS.B 8AccessName	DS.B 17DesParms		; 	DC.W Passbuffer+1	DC.W ReplyBuff+2	DC.W DesLogRes	if OSFlag =128 or OSFlag = 192 theninitparms	DC.B $00,$01,$00,$00 ;open the drivers	DC.B $40ProEntPt	DC.B $00,$00,$00,$00 ;past junk	DC.B $00	;pick a node, any node	DC.B $00,$00aiparms	DC.B $02,$00,$19,$c7setprint		; 	DC.B $00,$28,$00,$00PrName	DC.L 0theflag	DC.B $a0	;bit5 = ImageWriter	Emulation	DC.W 2	;Flush Buffer Timer	DC.W 15*4	;Session Timeout	DC.W 20	;number of buffers for RPMidtbl	DC.B 'ATLK'qMSG1LEN	str 'APPLETALK REQUIRES AN ENHANCED 'qmsg2len	str '128K APPLE IIE SYSTEM.'qmsg1	equ qMsg1Len+1qmsg2	equ qMsg2Len+1	EndIF	IF (OSFlag = 0) or (OSFlag = 128) or (OSFlag = 192) THEN;------------------------------------------;; ProDOS8 Parameter Lists;;------------------------------------------FOpen	DC.B $03	DC.W UserFName	DC.W IOBuff	DS.B 1FRead	DC.B $04RefNum	DS.B 1DataBuf	DC.W ReplyBuffReqCnt	DC.W $FFFFTranCnt	DS.B 2FWrite		; 	DC.B $04	DS.B 1	DC.W NameBuffer	DC.W 33	;write request count	DS.B 2FClose	DC.B $01	DS.B 1QuitParm	DC.B $04	;and we are done	DC.B $00	;	DS.B 3FlushParm	DC.B $01	;Parameter count	DS.B 1	;file reference numberSetPrefix		; 	DC.B $01	DC.W PrefixSetMarkParm	DC.B $02	DS.B 1	DS.B 3OnLineParm		; 	DC.B $02UnitNum	DS.B 1	DC.W ReplyBuffGetFInfoParm		; 	DC.B $0a	DS.B 17RBParm	DC.B $03RBUnitNum	DS.B 1	DC.W ReplyBuff	DC.W 0GetEofParm	DC.B $02	DS.B 1	DS.B 3	EndIF		IF OSFlag = 64 THEN;------------------------------------------;; ProDOS16 Parameter Lists;;------------------------------------------QuitParms	DC.L 0	; return to top of quit stack	DC.W 0	; never return to me	EndIF;------------------------------------------;; Strings;;------------------------------------------server		; 	str '='	str 'afpserver'ZoneName	str '*'	DS.B 31MyZone	str '*'NameField	Cstr 'Name: 'PassField	Cstr 'Password:'OldPassword	Cstr 'Old Password:'NewPassword	Cstr 'New Password:'SelectServ	Cstr 'Select a file server:'SelectVol	Cstr 'Mark the additional volume(s) you need:'ChoseZone	Cstr 'Select a new zone:'CurrZone	Cstr 'Current zone: '*** added 25-Nov-92 DALBuildZL	Cstr '  Looking for AppleTalk zones  '*** end 25-Nov-92FSLookUp	Cstr '  Looking for AFP file servers 'LaunchStart	Cstr ' Now launching the startup path:'UserDir	Cstr 'users/'GuestName	str '<Any User>'ClrText	str 'Cleartxt Passwrd'Guest	str 'No User Authent'RanExch	str 'Randnum Exchange'Entry1	str 'Log on as a Registered User'Entry2	str 'Log on as a Guest'Entry3	str 'Change Password'UserFName	str 'setup/atinit'P8FName	str 'atinit'P16FName	str 'system/system.setup/atinit'MailName	str 'Mail'LogonStr	str 'AFPVersion 2.0'LogOnSplash1	str 'Apple II File Server Log On V1.5  'LogOnSplash2	str 'Copyright Apple Computer, Inc.  1987-1992'LogOnSplash3	str 'All Rights Reserved'TwoEtype	str 'Apple IIe'GStype	str 'Apple IIgs';------------------------------------------;; Logon Variables;;------------------------------------------NoMoreVols	DS.B 1OtherSrvrFlg	DS.B 1	;Flag to indicate another server lookupDeriveCnt	DS.B 1NoNameFlag	DS.B 1CheckLog	DS.B 1CompTemp	DS.B 1CaseFlg	DS.B 1SkipFlag	DS.B 1BlockLen	DS.B 1DrawCnt	DS.B 1YPos	DS.B 1B_LNGTH	DS.B 1AuthFlag	DS.B 1EOFPntr	DS.B 2MySel	DS.B 1ZoneFlag	DS.B 1MovOffset	DS.B 1UserAuthFlag	DS.B 1OurVolSess	DS.B 1SelFlag	DS.B 1UMountFlag	DS.B 1OurSlotDrive	DS.B 1LogErrCnt	DS.B 1